1
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:16,558
What did you do?

2
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:18,184
Cheska!

3
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:19,769
It's Shane, isn't it?

4
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,605
I've already been screwed over,
and now you're making me look stupid?

5
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:23,690
What do you want from me?

6
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:25,859
- The truth!
- You can't handle it.

7
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:26,776
Liar!

8
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,528
It's the truth, Cisco!

9
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,280
I don't believe you!

10
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:33,116
You think that I cheated?

11
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:35,118
Can you accept that?

12
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,871
Do you even deserve my love?

13
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:51,468
Cisco…

14
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:45,647


15
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:52,987


16
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:54,989
Yes, Ms. Ana.

17
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:57,992
<i>Their final decision is</i>
<i>not to proceed with the DBS.</i>

18
00:01:58,076 --> 00:02:00,036
<i>- We're heading back to Singapore.</i>
- What? No, no, no!

19
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,746
I'll talk to them. I can convince them.

20
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:05,583
I'll be there around five.
6:00 AM latest, Ms. Ana.

21
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:10,713
Dad, can I use your car, please?

22
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,674
Wait, I'll check if our driver is back.

23
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:14,884
No, I don't need a driver. I can manage.

24
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:17,679
It's like a seven-to-eight-hour drive.

25
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,097
Did you even sleep last night?

26
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,140
I'm fine.

27
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,141
Please?

28
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:24,853
Isa, can I use your car?

29
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:27,188
- Fran?
- Dad?

30
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:28,815
No.

31
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,192
The last time you drove,
your car was a wreck.

32
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,443
It was an accident!

33
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:35,155
I was not trying to kill myself!

34
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:37,323
Son.

35
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:41,911
I know how difficult it is
to move on after a relationship--

36
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:42,954
Really?

37
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:45,290
You had a hard time?

38
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,376
Cisco!

39
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:50,044
I'll just find my own ride.

40
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:16,195
JC.

41
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,614
My love!

42
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:19,073
You forgot the keys.

43
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,283
Oh!

44
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:22,327
My heart!

45
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,703
Thank you!

46
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:25,538
Sorry about that.

47
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:27,874
We're newlyweds.

48
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,586
Oh, right.

49
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:33,922
This is my wife, Lisa.

50
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:36,966
Cisco, meet Lisa.

51
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:40,720
Cisco? Isn't he--?

52
00:03:40,803 --> 00:03:42,805
Uh…

53
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,474
My heart!

54
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:47,393
You left the stove on.
You should go check on it.

55
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:48,937
But I'm not cooking anything, love.

56
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,521
Well, cook something!

57
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:52,982
I'm hungry. Your husband is hungry.

58
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:55,526
- Okay.
- Bye.

59
00:03:57,987 --> 00:04:01,282
Too bad you and Cheska missed our wedding.

60
00:04:02,116 --> 00:04:04,202
You guys inspired me to find love.

61
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,246
The keys, JC?

62
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:10,917
Wait. Don't you want to shave?

63
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,087
I know you want to look like me, but

64
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:18,132
Cheska won't take you back
if you look like that.

65
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,592
The keys.

66
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:29,269
Remember,

67
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:31,854
I love you.

68
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:37,485
But I love my new car more.

69
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:40,154
Take care of it.

70
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:43,366
Return it with a full tank
and charged, okay?

71
00:04:43,992 --> 00:04:45,702
Does it have those now?

72
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:46,786
Of course not!

73
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:48,329
You just borrowed it now.

74
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:51,749
Thanks.

75
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:55,837
All right. Just press the key,
and you'll find it.

76
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,880
My car is as handsome as me.

77
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,025
Hi, ex.

78
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:19,736
- No.
- Definitely not.

79
00:05:19,819 --> 00:05:20,987
That's why it's an X.

80
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:25,158
As your ex, I say big red "X"
to whatever you're planning.

81
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,786
Not now. I'm in a hurry.

82
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:32,749
Exactly why I'm rushing to stop you.

83
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:34,292
Why are you doing this?

84
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,668
Why are you doing this?

85
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:36,836
You know why.

86
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:40,465
Honestly, I don't.

87
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:42,967
Because to be honest,
you don't have the right anymore.

88
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,469
We're not doing this now.

89
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:48,056
Ooh. That sounded like a command.

90
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:50,516
I say we do the breakup trip.

91
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,019
Please go away.

92
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:54,729
Not until we do the breakup trip.

93
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,397
There you go again.

94
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:57,690
No!

95
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:59,150
There you go again.

96
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:00,193
Yes!

97
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,031
Cisco,

98
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,909
why do you keep delaying the inevitable?

99
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:09,702
So annoying!

100
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,621
It's been almost two years.

101
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:13,247
Let's do the breakup trip!

102
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:15,458
I'm going somewhere more important.

103
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:18,920
Look, we both need to move on.

104
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:21,547
If you do this with me, I'll shut up.

105
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:22,507
For good.

106
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:26,886
Let's do this!

107
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:30,056
Breakup trip! Breakup trip!

108
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:31,724
Breakup trip!

109
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,309
Breakup trip!

110
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:38,564
Mm? Why didn't you pin Mt. Polis?

111
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,733
That's the endpoint of our breakup trip.

112
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:43,986
We agreed to do
the breakup trip before we--

113
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,905
I did not agree.

114
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:47,657
I just knew you wouldn't leave me alone.

115
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,033
Not fair.

116
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:49,992
Shhh.

117
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:57,583
See? They're not answering.

118
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,961
It only means one thing.

119
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:06,050
That's the call that you should take!

120
00:07:10,179 --> 00:07:11,013
Hey!

121
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:12,557
That's your mom!

122
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,891
She's offering you a job.

123
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,601
You can start over in Australia--

124
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:17,937
I don't want to be a nepo baby.

125
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:20,106
Set your pride aside. You need this.

126
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:22,233
What I need is for people to believe me.

127
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:24,527
I need them to see there is hope,
there is still a chance--

128
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:26,612
That's not what you want.

129
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:29,657
All you want is control.
You have to get your way.

130
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,868
If I'm right, why shouldn't I?

131
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:34,203
Some things just never change.

132
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:37,874
You're still the same pushy guy who will
do everything just to get your way.

133
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:39,000
No, I'm not.

134
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:40,960
- Who only cares about winning!
- Stop!

135
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:43,337
- You know nothing's gonna change--
- Stop being pessimistic!

136
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:46,257
I'm just being realistic!
As you should be!

137
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,968
So you should go to Australia and move on.

138
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:50,136
I refuse to move on!

139
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:51,846
Oh, what a line!

140
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:53,973
- You're expecting to get back--
- Stop!

141
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,685
You know,
for someone trying to win their ex back,

142
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:59,103
you're the grumpiest.

143
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,063
So gloomy. And you look like you smell.

144
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:03,733
I'm not trying to get back together.

145
00:08:03,816 --> 00:08:05,318
We're still together.

146
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:10,239
Do I need to remind you
yet again how it ended?

147
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:14,076
I'd rather remember
why we should never end.

148
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,579
Fine.

149
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:18,581
Then tell me. Why?

150
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,376
Do we have to start where it began?

151
00:08:23,961 --> 00:08:25,046
No.

152
00:08:25,129 --> 00:08:27,048
I know what you're trying to do.

153
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,382
You can't fool me.

154
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:30,760
This is not a breakup trip.

155
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,640
<i> I told the board</i>

156
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:38,100
that these two will run
our integrated content lab.

157
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,769
They said I lost my mind.

158
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:42,855
"Your Gen Z prodigies do not know crap

159
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:45,650
about running this business,
so prepare to crash!"

160
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,443
We proved them wrong.

161
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:50,947
We are opening our own division!

162
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:55,993
So, boys, what do we call it?

163
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:56,994
Hmm?

164
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:58,371
Gold Minds.

165
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:00,706
It keeps the Guinto Group brand.

166
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:05,795
Gold standards.
Gold ideas. Gold minds.

167
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:07,296
I like that.

168
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,298
Not bad.

169
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:12,134
But for an attention economy,

170
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,637
we need a name that people will remember.

171
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,682
We're here to blow minds, guys.

172
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:20,309
We are here to keep the tradition.

173
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:22,645
The culture of excellence.

174
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:24,772
Then why make something new?

175
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:27,024
We have to disrupt the system, guys.

176
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:28,150
That's why we're here.

177
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,987
We will find that perfect spot
in our clients' brands.

178
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,989
Audience. Stories.

179
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,240
They have to connect!

180
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:36,242
The G Spot!

181
00:09:36,325 --> 00:09:40,371
Oh my.

182
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:42,707
Kinky!

183
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:47,295
Witty.

184
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,884
- Guys, meet our new intern.
- Hi everyone!

185
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,595
She was my best student at CST.

186
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:58,472
OMG! You're the new housemate
Mr. G mentioned?

187
00:09:58,556 --> 00:10:00,308
I believe we have a name!

188
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,226
The G Spot!

189
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:04,854
Good job, boys! Good job!

190
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,896
Amazing!

191
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,231
Congratulations.

192
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:15,865
Let me get a tumbler I can lend you.

193
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:16,866
Okay.

194
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,634
Yes!

195
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,260
G Spot!

196
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:38,304
G Spot. G Spot.

197
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:55,863
Here it is!

198
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:57,531
Uh…

199
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:58,574
Smells like rotten eggs.

200
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,617
More like poop!

201
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:01,911
Really?

202
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:07,041
- I smell nothing.
- Me too.

203
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:10,795
Just find me at my table.

204
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:23,391
How embarrassing.

205
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:26,227
Totally human.

206
00:11:28,187 --> 00:11:29,355
Thanks.

207
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:34,985
Francisco Serrano.

208
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:37,947
Cisco.

209
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:42,243
Francisca Alegre.

210
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:44,453
Cisca?

211
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,623
Let's make it classier.

212
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:48,541
Cheska.

213
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:50,209
Oh.

214
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:51,544
Two of a kind!

215
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:53,170
Call me Tuks!

216
00:11:57,466 --> 00:11:59,718
- That's their PR spin.
- Ugh, what a hassle.

217
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:02,054
They say his fiancée's just jealous.

218
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:07,184
- But she has proof.
- Their careers can't survive this scandal.

219
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:09,019
- Guys!
- Boss.

220
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,480
Dolce Bravo Ice Cream is in panic mode!

221
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:13,649
They need solutions in two hours.

222
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:16,944
Do we still push through
with Jesse and Andy's campaign?

223
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:19,488
Sir, I don't think we should
push through with this.

224
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:24,118
A celebrity's cheating scandal
won't die down in just two days.

225
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:26,328
They will ruin
the Dolce Bravo brand.

226
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:27,955
I say we still push through.

227
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:28,789
Huh?

228
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,208
We already have placements and hype.

229
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,627
If we pull out now,
the brand loses momentum.

230
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:35,671
Same strategy.

231
00:12:35,754 --> 00:12:37,548
Just different faces.

232
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:43,387
What if we get the couple
who sing while cooking?

233
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,639
That won't work for the older market.

234
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:46,932
What if we get a solo artist?

235
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,267
But a big star!

236
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:50,102
- Great idea, right?
- Tina!

237
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:54,607
The whole product feature is a combination
of two ice cream flavors.

238
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:56,901
I need viable options, guys!
Come on, guys, think!

239
00:12:56,984 --> 00:13:00,029
We need a love team that appeals
across generations.

240
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,322
A wholesome love team.

241
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:04,116
And please, with no scandals, okay?

242
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:06,535
- Boss!
- Yes?

243
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:08,746
Other boss.

244
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,917
I think Tina's idea could work--

245
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,502
I just said--

246
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:22,051
What if we get one star
who can carry two flavors?

247
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:25,930
Light and pure as vanilla
and as intense as dark chocolate.

248
00:13:26,013 --> 00:13:28,599
A star that can make you feel two ways.

249
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:31,393
Both sweet and bold.

250
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,394
Like who?

251
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:34,396
Giuliarose.

252
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:37,233
She can do romcom. She can do drama.

253
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:39,777
That why she's called the Queen of Feels.

254
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:43,239
So you're saying,
why get two different tubs of ice cream…

255
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:45,616
If you can get them in one.

256
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:47,868
Okay!

257
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:48,953
Let's make a teaser.

258
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:51,330
- You'll stand in for Giuliarose.
- I can assist as well.

259
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:52,540
- You'll edit this.
- Yes, sir.

260
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,166
- What about the music?
- Same as before.

261
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,502
Perfect! We'll make a deck
with the proposed execution.

262
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,087
Then set a meeting for client approval.

263
00:13:58,170 --> 00:13:59,338
Then we can shoot tomorrow.

264
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:01,006
We just need to inform Giuliarose's team.

265
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:02,091
I'm on it.

266
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:03,717
Now that's the perfect pair.

267
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:05,886
You two should be the new love team.

268
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,888
Hey, include us too. We're right here.

269
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:09,974
<i> To G Spot!</i>

270
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:15,396
Cisco!

271
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:17,856
- Keep it up!
- Thank you, Mr. G!

272
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,901
- Cisco, let's take a picture!
- Okay!

273
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,237
Okay.

274
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,781
- I'll go ahead.
- All right, be safe!

275
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,659
- Hey!
- Oh no, it's broken.

276
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:31,662
Cisco!

277
00:14:31,745 --> 00:14:33,706
Take a picture with me too!

278
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:37,793
Let's take a groufie.

279
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,795
Yeah!

280
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:43,966
Leave Cisco alone, you guys!

281
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,260
- Let's go?
- Ready when you are.

282
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:47,595
Tuks!

283
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:49,972
Leaving already?

284
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:52,725
Yes. I'm hitching a ride with Shane.

285
00:14:52,808 --> 00:14:54,310
Stay. I'll take you home instead.

286
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:55,978
I'll get you a drink!

287
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:58,188
No need. I have a lot to do anyway.

288
00:14:58,272 --> 00:14:59,481
Thank you, though.

289
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:00,524
Let's go?

290
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:07,406
Are you giving up already?

291
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:08,407
Huh?

292
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,492
On the drinks, I mean. Drink more!

293
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:12,745
Cheers!

294
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:15,623
Hmmm.

295
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,227
Have you eaten, Cheska?

296
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:39,229
Not yet.

297
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:40,814
Come on, let's eat.

298
00:15:42,816 --> 00:15:44,443
- You okay?
- Yes.

299
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:51,116
Are you really going home
to your province tonight?

300
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,118
Yes. I have a lot of stuff to do.

301
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:55,245
But it's so late.
Isn't it dangerous?

302
00:15:55,329 --> 00:15:57,122
I'm used to it.

303
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:59,583
Just text me
when you get home, okay?

304
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,293
Okay. I'll just take the bus.

305
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:03,545
- I can't find my phone.
- I'm sure it's there.

306
00:16:04,505 --> 00:16:06,340
Hey. Cisco! Are you okay?

307
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:10,302
Today's extra tiring.

308
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:13,180
I know. So much work!

309
00:16:16,016 --> 00:16:17,935
- Cisco!
- Are you okay?

310
00:16:18,018 --> 00:16:20,229
- Hey.
- Oh my goodness.

311
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,690
I'm okay.

312
00:16:25,859 --> 00:16:27,277
Thank you, guys!

313
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:29,446
- Are you okay?
- Yes. I don't know.

314
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:33,283
I tripped over my own foot.

315
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:41,792
I have the exact same one!

316
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:44,795
Mm?

317
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:46,714
- Yes.
- This one?

318
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:51,760
No freaking way!

319
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:54,138
We really are two of a kind!

320
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,099
Bam!

321
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:00,978
I'll take you home.

322
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:04,273
But I'm going home to my parents'.

323
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:06,650
That's okay.

324
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:09,778
It's a three-hour drive.

325
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,030
Oh.

326
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:13,991
Okay.

327
00:17:15,909 --> 00:17:16,910
Okay.

328
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,246
Here they go again.

329
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:22,124
- They're fighting again!
- It's going to be a long night!

330
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:25,294
Let's sit back and
enjoy our regular show.

331
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:29,256
She's thrown the whole
kitchen at him already.

332
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:35,846
Cheska! We're about to get
to the good part!

333
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:38,098
My timing is perfect!

334
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:41,143
- Take this, you lazy idiot!
- Please, stop!

335
00:17:41,226 --> 00:17:43,312
- Big bro!
- Go be with your friends!

336
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:45,147
- Take your roosters with you!
- Oh hey!

337
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:47,941
- This will take another hour, right?
- They give me work!

338
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,193
More or less.

339
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:51,236
Mom has more plates to throw.

340
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,529
Fine, we'll go--

341
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,656
Oh! Hey, Cisco! Come here!

342
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,783
Who's this?

343
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:56,742
My officemate.

344
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:57,910
Wow, he's tall.

345
00:17:57,993 --> 00:17:59,828
- My name's Rafa.
- Cisco.

346
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:04,249
- We'll be right back.
- Sure, I'll message you when they're done.

347
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,876
- Sure you can handle it?
- Yes.

348
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:09,546
They're my bosses!
I need to get along with them.

349
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,341
We can't even afford rent!
Let's just go back to the province!

350
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:14,468
- This is me.
- That's too far.

351
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:17,304
You need to be separated
from your gambler friends.

352
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:18,472
It's cold there.

353
00:18:18,555 --> 00:18:20,849
You and your roosters
can freeze there.

354
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:27,648
It's okay.

355
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:30,150
Don't be embarrassed.

356
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:36,573
Dude! I just have a headache.

357
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:41,203
Why would I be embarrassed?

358
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,539
It's normal for couples to fight.

359
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,541
No, it's not.

360
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:48,836
Your parents never fight?

361
00:18:50,003 --> 00:18:50,921
No.

362
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:55,801
They're separated. How would they fight?

363
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:59,179
Are you serious?

364
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,434
It's true!

365
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:08,105
I guess I win.

366
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:09,148
Oh?

367
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,441
Is that a challenge?

368
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,110
Yes.

369
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,570
Okay.

370
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:18,657
My dad's been gambling since I was two.

371
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:20,576
My mom left me when I was two.

372
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:22,452
She chose Australia.

373
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:26,582
My mom has been playing dumb for 20 years.
She won't leave my dad.

374
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:30,085
My dad had a new family
in less than 20 days.

375
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:33,422
So

376
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:35,841
I no longer have a family.

377
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:43,515
Let's start a family.

378
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:45,934
You wish!

379
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:57,529
This is me.

380
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:01,491
This is us.

381
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:16,048
Good morning!

382
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:17,382
They're a couple!

383
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:28,769
You didn't tell me you were
coming out as a couple today!

384
00:20:28,852 --> 00:20:31,230
So, sir, are you now moving in with us?

385
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:32,189
Maybe.

386
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:35,275
- You guys!
- Congratulations!

387
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:42,407
As of today, officially,
Cheska is regularized!

388
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:45,410
Oh my God!

389
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:48,372
- Thank you, sir!
- Thank you, sir!

390
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:51,500
And… congratulations!

391
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:56,588
It may not be forbidden,

392
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:58,298
but keep it professional.

393
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,217
- Yes, sir.
- Promise, sir.

394
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,971
It could get complicated and ugly.

395
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,556
I've seen it happen!

396
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,022
But who knows?

397
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,774
Maybe your story will end differently.

398
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:19,236
We won't have an ending, sir.

399
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:20,279
Right?

400
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,331
Is that a smile?

401
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:34,668
You're smiling!

402
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:37,170
I thought you didn't want
to do the breakup trip.

403
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,880
Guess you gave in.

404
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:41,591
You talk too much.

405
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:44,803
So you were listening to my stories?

406
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:46,888
- This is a breakup trip.
- No, it's not.

407
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:48,432
Okay, fine.

408
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:51,310
But don't hide that smile.

409
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:53,061
You were right.

410
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:56,148
It felt almost serendipitous.

411
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:57,858
Magical.

412
00:21:59,109 --> 00:22:00,235
Not almost.

413
00:22:02,279 --> 00:22:03,447
It really was.

414
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,993
I meant it when I said
we'd have no ending.

415
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:12,289
But there's no such thing.

416
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:15,876
All must come to an end.

417
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:17,961
- There you go again.
- Okay, okay.

418
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:20,672
Let's go back to the part
where you were smiling.

419
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:21,882
Where were we?

420
00:22:29,514 --> 00:22:30,849
I just miss us.

421
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:34,811
The old Cheska.

422
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:39,691
Who didn't ask for much?

423
00:22:41,985 --> 00:22:43,361
Who didn't need much?

424
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:03,423
Can I carry all of this in one go?

425
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,133
Nope. The fragile ones first.

426
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:07,094
Tuks! Are we ready?

427
00:23:07,177 --> 00:23:08,553
We are!

428
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:12,474
- Let's go, let's go!
- I'll get these.

429
00:23:12,557 --> 00:23:14,643
Just roll with his mood swings.

430
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:16,186
You know how artists are.

431
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:18,522
But JC is nice.

432
00:23:25,862 --> 00:23:26,780
Cisco.

433
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:31,493
This is the way.

434
00:23:33,703 --> 00:23:34,538
Come in!

435
00:23:34,621 --> 00:23:35,705
- Let's go.
- You were right.

436
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:36,706
Told you.

437
00:23:38,542 --> 00:23:40,961
Cheska! This is it!

438
00:23:41,044 --> 00:23:43,338
- Tina.
- Boss! We're housemates now.

439
00:23:43,421 --> 00:23:45,465
- Let me help you.
- I got it. They're fragile.

440
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:47,884
Cheska, let's switch roomies.
You can have Tina.

441
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:48,885
- Hello.
- Behave.

442
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:49,886
Hi, bro.

443
00:23:50,428 --> 00:23:52,848
- Cisco.
- I'm Bonj.

444
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:54,432
Hi, Cheska.

445
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:55,809
Hi!

446
00:23:56,601 --> 00:23:58,687
Should I come back tomorrow?

447
00:23:58,770 --> 00:24:00,522
- Who is she?
- She's a regular.

448
00:24:00,605 --> 00:24:02,232
- A regular what?
- I'll think about it.

449
00:24:02,315 --> 00:24:04,151
You were like a starfish last night.

450
00:24:14,327 --> 00:24:16,288
Tukie, help!

451
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:17,873
Tukie!

452
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:21,418
I can't reach it.

453
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:28,300
Beautiful.

454
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:30,552
Tukie, the curtains will fall.

455
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:32,888
No, it's fine. Keep going.
You're tall anyway.

456
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:36,099
I can't reach it.
That's why I need you.

457
00:24:41,938 --> 00:24:44,065
Oh!

458
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,786
Come here!

459
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:13,637
You think you can escape me?

460
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:17,599
Tuks…

461
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:20,227
Not now! Later!

462
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:36,409
Come here.

463
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:39,871
Oh, you.

464
00:26:00,058 --> 00:26:02,143
Are you guys sure about this?

465
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:05,355
'Cause it's a lot!

466
00:26:13,947 --> 00:26:15,156
Do you regret it?

467
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:17,826
Living together?

468
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:23,623
I actually don't think regret
is the right word.

469
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:25,667
Maybe it was just

470
00:26:26,584 --> 00:26:28,211
too much too soon.

471
00:26:29,546 --> 00:26:32,424
Well, living together
seemed right at that time.

472
00:26:34,217 --> 00:26:37,387
Practical. Convenient.

473
00:26:39,139 --> 00:26:40,765
Shared expenses.

474
00:26:40,849 --> 00:26:42,642
It helped us financially.

475
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:46,646
But, yeah.

476
00:26:47,397 --> 00:26:48,773
Emotionally…

477
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:52,360
It cost us a lot.

478
00:27:00,243 --> 00:27:01,411
You're anxious.

479
00:27:03,538 --> 00:27:04,998
Am I?

480
00:27:05,081 --> 00:27:05,957
Mm.

481
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:09,544
This is why I don't want to look back.

482
00:27:09,627 --> 00:27:12,172
- The past?
- You're so annoying! Shh!

483
00:27:12,714 --> 00:27:13,590
Just shut up!

484
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:24,476
That's so emo.

485
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:44,245
This is so annoying.

486
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:52,587
Fate is funny sometimes, huh?

487
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:56,049
<i>♪ If you want this to end ♪</i>

488
00:27:56,132 --> 00:27:58,176
<i>♪ Then just say so ♪</i>

489
00:28:01,596 --> 00:28:04,349
<i>♪ If you want this to stop-- ♪</i>

490
00:28:04,432 --> 00:28:06,309
Stop! Shut up!

491
00:28:14,109 --> 00:28:15,902
What if we actually broke up?

492
00:28:21,825 --> 00:28:26,496
Tuks! Change your shirt
so you can convince the client.

493
00:28:26,579 --> 00:28:27,747
Is that really necessary?

494
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:30,458
Of course! You're the brains
behind the campaign.

495
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,876
The future is orange.

496
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:35,088
"Orange" you a little excited?

497
00:28:35,171 --> 00:28:36,047
Of course!

498
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:38,425
You're getting Garcia the presidency!

499
00:28:38,508 --> 00:28:40,593
"Orange" you proud of me?

500
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:41,511
Great!

501
00:28:41,594 --> 00:28:43,221
Let's go, Madam President!

502
00:28:43,304 --> 00:28:45,056
National average for all three metrics

503
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:47,350
is 30% or lower.

504
00:28:47,434 --> 00:28:48,893
Are you serious?

505
00:28:49,477 --> 00:28:51,062
Are your results accurate?

506
00:28:51,146 --> 00:28:53,732
Consistent across multiple runs.

507
00:28:54,315 --> 00:28:58,445
In conclusion, all three taglines
scored below 50% nationwide

508
00:28:58,528 --> 00:29:00,488
across all markets.

509
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:03,199
So, it still works.

510
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:06,494
Yes. For people like you
in team G Spot.

511
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:09,748
Urban, educated, high purchasing power…

512
00:29:09,831 --> 00:29:11,833
Advocacy-driven.

513
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:15,462
But we agreed to target the masses.

514
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:17,797
They're the priority, remember?

515
00:29:17,881 --> 00:29:20,425
Meanwhile, the strongest
opponent nationwide…

516
00:29:20,508 --> 00:29:22,010
Their most effective taglines are:

517
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:23,636
"Affordable Rice,"

518
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:25,054
"Housing for All,"

519
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:27,223
and "Affordable Onions."

520
00:29:27,307 --> 00:29:29,976
These taglines resonate with more people.

521
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:32,604
Even if they know it's all a lie?

522
00:29:32,687 --> 00:29:33,563
Yes.

523
00:29:33,646 --> 00:29:35,690
That's what sticks.

524
00:29:35,774 --> 00:29:39,152
Okay. Let's change direction.

525
00:29:39,235 --> 00:29:41,362
Wait, sir.

526
00:29:41,446 --> 00:29:43,198
We can't just change
our strategy like that.

527
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:45,992
Our taglines are built on truth.

528
00:29:46,075 --> 00:29:48,369
This shows exactly who our candidate is.

529
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:50,789
And yet it's not working.

530
00:29:50,872 --> 00:29:52,207
With all due respect,

531
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:55,794
our entire campaign is built on integrity.

532
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:57,921
Long-term trust.

533
00:29:58,004 --> 00:30:03,301
With all due respect,
you won't win if nobody's listening.

534
00:30:03,384 --> 00:30:06,763
Can we at least test them again
before we kill the idea completely?

535
00:30:07,430 --> 00:30:09,682
- Cheska.
- Mr. G?

536
00:30:09,766 --> 00:30:12,644
When you go home to your province,

537
00:30:12,727 --> 00:30:14,521
what do you usually hear?

538
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:16,815
Hmm…

539
00:30:21,194 --> 00:30:25,865
They don't really talk about
decent public service

540
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:28,159
or the future.

541
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:32,121
Mostly, they talk about rent,

542
00:30:32,205 --> 00:30:34,582
water bills, electricity bills,

543
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:36,584
fares, tuition fees,

544
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:40,463
and how they wish food was cheaper.

545
00:30:40,547 --> 00:30:43,633
Even I worry if my salary
will last the month,

546
00:30:43,716 --> 00:30:46,469
or if I can still send money back home.

547
00:30:47,512 --> 00:30:50,139
Bingo! That's the direction I want.

548
00:30:52,892 --> 00:30:55,728
But "The Future is Orange"
is good too, sir.

549
00:30:55,812 --> 00:30:58,773
Enough with the orange antics.

550
00:31:03,778 --> 00:31:05,405
We're working late again tonight!

551
00:31:05,488 --> 00:31:07,198
- Yup!
- Not again.

552
00:31:07,282 --> 00:31:10,076
You Gen Z kids think
you're the only voters--

553
00:31:10,159 --> 00:31:12,120
What about us?

554
00:31:17,166 --> 00:31:18,710
Let's sit here.

555
00:31:32,348 --> 00:31:33,683
Are we okay?

556
00:31:34,559 --> 00:31:35,476
Huh?

557
00:31:36,185 --> 00:31:37,145
Yes.

558
00:31:39,105 --> 00:31:39,939
Tuks…

559
00:31:40,732 --> 00:31:41,900
- I'm sorry if--
- No.

560
00:31:45,612 --> 00:31:47,238
You were just being honest.

561
00:31:49,157 --> 00:31:50,241
Okay?

562
00:31:52,994 --> 00:31:54,329
Come on. Let's eat.

563
00:31:55,455 --> 00:31:56,748
"Orange" you mad?

564
00:32:02,211 --> 00:32:05,673
"Orange" you a little paranoid?

565
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:09,052
"Orange" you sweet?

566
00:32:19,729 --> 00:32:21,064
I love you, Tuks.

567
00:32:22,148 --> 00:32:23,107
I love you more.

568
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:25,443
I love you more, more, more, more, more.

569
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:28,905
No, I love you more, more, more, more,
more, more, more, more.

570
00:32:30,573 --> 00:32:34,702
When things aren't going well,
people turn to ice cream…

571
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:36,829
That's where Dolce Bravo enters.

572
00:32:37,997 --> 00:32:40,458
Maybe go straight to the point, Tuks.

573
00:32:40,541 --> 00:32:42,502
- Okay. Tina, kindly note please.
- Copy.

574
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:44,212
We're staying at Mom's
for one night, right?

575
00:32:44,295 --> 00:32:46,839
Two nights. We'll head there
right after your presentation.

576
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,466
- Come on, girl!
- Hmm?

577
00:32:48,549 --> 00:32:51,886
Giuliarose has a bad image now.
Why should we keep her?

578
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:56,099
We should keep her because--
Needs more vinegar!

579
00:32:56,766 --> 00:32:58,101
Tukie! Tukie!

580
00:32:58,184 --> 00:33:00,395
I got this.

581
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:01,646
Look at me. Hey.

582
00:33:02,271 --> 00:33:04,107
Focus on the pitch, okay?

583
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:05,858
We have to prove Giuliarose to the client.

584
00:33:05,942 --> 00:33:08,403
We cannot lose Dolce Bravo.

585
00:33:08,486 --> 00:33:09,612
That account is ours.

586
00:33:10,822 --> 00:33:14,283
We have to be present
even during the bad days--

587
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:16,869
No! That's awful!

588
00:33:18,371 --> 00:33:19,205
It's awful?

589
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:24,877
No, I meant this.
I punched the holes wrong.

590
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:27,296
- It looks awful.
- Don't mind him. Continue.

591
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:29,298
Tuks…

592
00:33:30,383 --> 00:33:31,759
can I really do this?

593
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,845
Maybe you should do the presentation?

594
00:33:34,429 --> 00:33:37,348
Tuks, you can do it.

595
00:33:38,391 --> 00:33:41,644
And Cheska, you were trained by the best.

596
00:33:50,945 --> 00:33:52,321
You got this!

597
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:54,824
I got this.

598
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:58,494
Ice cream has always been about

599
00:33:58,578 --> 00:34:01,247
more than just perfectly sweet moments.

600
00:34:01,330 --> 00:34:05,209
In fact, people turn to ice cream
when things are not perfect.

601
00:34:05,293 --> 00:34:09,714
When life gets messy,
stressful, and complicated.

602
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:12,091
We're an ice cream brand.

603
00:34:12,175 --> 00:34:14,260
A family brand. We should stay wholesome.

604
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:16,429
Giuliarose isn't wholesome anymore.

605
00:34:16,512 --> 00:34:18,806
So why are you insisting on keeping her?

606
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:20,558
We also learned that consumers

607
00:34:20,641 --> 00:34:22,727
don't support Giuliarose anymore.

608
00:34:22,810 --> 00:34:24,604
And you still want to keep her?

609
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:25,897
A bad girl?

610
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:30,234
But Dolce Bravo
was never just about being good.

611
00:34:30,318 --> 00:34:32,320
Or for the good ones.

612
00:34:32,403 --> 00:34:34,363
But it's also about comfort,

613
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:36,282
regardless if you're good or bad.

614
00:34:36,866 --> 00:34:38,367
The brand sticks with her.

615
00:34:38,993 --> 00:34:40,328
With us.

616
00:34:40,411 --> 00:34:41,996
Not just when you're at your best

617
00:34:42,997 --> 00:34:45,875
but especially when you're not.

618
00:34:51,255 --> 00:34:53,216
Why is Cheska a little moody?

619
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:55,885
She's just tired from the trip.

620
00:35:17,532 --> 00:35:18,616
Are you okay?

621
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:21,327
You were quiet the whole ride.

622
00:35:21,994 --> 00:35:24,205
I thought I was alone.
You were pretending to sleep.

623
00:35:24,997 --> 00:35:26,499
You didn't even get me a drink.

624
00:35:28,417 --> 00:35:30,044
What? Is this about the pitch?

625
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:32,421
I was just trying to help.

626
00:35:32,505 --> 00:35:34,632
- I didn't need your help.
- You obviously did.

627
00:35:34,715 --> 00:35:36,843
If I'd needed your help,
I'd have let you know.

628
00:35:36,926 --> 00:35:38,427
The client was getting agitated.

629
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:41,347
- You were taking too long to answer.
- Seriously? That was just a beat.

630
00:35:41,430 --> 00:35:43,057
Can't I gather my thoughts for a second?

631
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,560
That's called dead air.
You cannot have dead air.

632
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:48,062
I was gonna say something.
You just cut in.

633
00:35:48,146 --> 00:35:49,522
Just admit you don't trust me enough.

634
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:54,318
I wouldn't have made you lead the pitch
if I didn't trust you.

635
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:56,821
Okay. Then why did you hijack
my presentation, huh?

636
00:35:56,904 --> 00:35:59,532
- I was saving you--
- I did not need saving!

637
00:35:59,615 --> 00:36:01,367
I will always save you.
You're my girlfriend!

638
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:04,579
Wow. I don't even know who I'm talking to
right now, my boyfriend or my boss?

639
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:05,538
Both!

640
00:36:06,122 --> 00:36:09,083
I always will care for you
as my girlfriend and my subordinate.

641
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:10,543
I want you to succeed!

642
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:12,545
With what you did,
you're the only one who succeeded.

643
00:36:12,628 --> 00:36:14,505
You made me look incompetent!

644
00:36:14,589 --> 00:36:17,091
Both of us will look incompetent
if I didn't save you.

645
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:20,469
Oh, so my mistake is going to
be yours, huh?!

646
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:21,387
Of course!

647
00:36:21,470 --> 00:36:22,805
Command responsibility.

648
00:36:22,889 --> 00:36:24,891
- I'm done!
- Me too!

649
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:26,684
- Copycat!
- Whatever! Goodbye!

650
00:36:26,767 --> 00:36:28,477
Goodbye? That's it?

651
00:36:29,270 --> 00:36:30,354
Did you hear that, Mr. G?

652
00:36:30,438 --> 00:36:32,732
Of course! Even Sally heard it.

653
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:36,903
- Hey, I'll get the usual.
- Okay, sir.

654
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:38,696
Mr. G, who has a point between us?

655
00:36:38,779 --> 00:36:39,614
Hmm.

656
00:36:39,697 --> 00:36:43,701
I believe you both have a point.

657
00:36:44,535 --> 00:36:46,412
And it showed in the results because…

658
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:48,497
we still got the account.

659
00:36:48,581 --> 00:36:50,833
- Congratulations!
- Yay!

660
00:36:54,837 --> 00:36:57,173
You want to celebrate at my place?

661
00:36:57,256 --> 00:36:59,383
We're going to Mt. Polis.
You should come with us, Mr. G.

662
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:01,928
Oh no. My knees.

663
00:37:02,011 --> 00:37:04,388
You can go ahead.

664
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:06,891
But leave now
if you want to catch the sea of clouds.

665
00:37:06,974 --> 00:37:08,684
The sea of clouds! Thank you, Mr. G!

666
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:10,394
Stop by the rest house
on your way back, okay?

667
00:37:10,478 --> 00:37:14,482
- Cheska, say hi to your parents for me!
- Okay, boss!

668
00:37:24,283 --> 00:37:25,701
Did we break up?

669
00:37:27,954 --> 00:37:28,996
Kind of.

670
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:31,624
But are we okay now?

671
00:37:36,837 --> 00:37:38,047
Shortest breakup ever.

672
00:37:38,130 --> 00:37:39,715
Let's never do that again.

673
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:40,675
Never.

674
00:37:40,758 --> 00:37:42,593
That hurt even if it was just quick.

675
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:43,970
Agreed.

676
00:37:44,053 --> 00:37:45,930
Never again.

677
00:37:46,013 --> 00:37:47,640
Here's the pitch.

678
00:37:50,309 --> 00:37:51,686
A breakup trip.

679
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:55,106
You mean like breakup sex?

680
00:37:55,189 --> 00:37:56,524
No. That complicates things.

681
00:37:56,607 --> 00:37:57,984
This is the opposite.

682
00:37:59,151 --> 00:38:00,319
How about this?

683
00:38:00,403 --> 00:38:02,989
If, only if,

684
00:38:03,072 --> 00:38:06,409
one or both of us
wants to quit the relationship,

685
00:38:06,492 --> 00:38:07,868
no running away.

686
00:38:08,411 --> 00:38:10,579
No leaving without an explanation.

687
00:38:11,247 --> 00:38:12,540
No ghosting.

688
00:38:12,623 --> 00:38:15,167
No goodbye texts or DMs.

689
00:38:15,251 --> 00:38:16,419
Exactly.

690
00:38:16,502 --> 00:38:18,671
No quiet quitting, slow fading,

691
00:38:18,754 --> 00:38:21,090
soft blocking, r-bombing,

692
00:38:21,173 --> 00:38:24,218
love droughting, orbiting,
submarining, zombie-ing!

693
00:38:26,887 --> 00:38:28,806
So that we don't do to each other…

694
00:38:28,889 --> 00:38:29,807
Smile.

695
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:33,978
…what my parents did to me.

696
00:38:36,105 --> 00:38:37,148
Okay?

697
00:38:38,190 --> 00:38:39,108
Never.

698
00:38:39,608 --> 00:38:44,405
So if ever we do want to end things,

699
00:38:45,281 --> 00:38:47,074
we don't just walk away,

700
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:49,452
we don't just disappear.

701
00:38:50,369 --> 00:38:51,245
We drive.

702
00:38:52,455 --> 00:38:53,539
To?

703
00:38:53,622 --> 00:38:55,374
Here, of course.

704
00:38:56,250 --> 00:38:58,919
Maybe we'll catch the sea of clouds then.

705
00:38:59,003 --> 00:39:00,588
There's none right now.

706
00:39:01,672 --> 00:39:03,632
So, a long drive?

707
00:39:03,716 --> 00:39:06,677
Let's give each other time
to make sense of our decision

708
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:08,304
and what happened to us.

709
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:10,765
No unanswered questions.

710
00:39:10,848 --> 00:39:11,974
No what-ifs.

711
00:39:13,476 --> 00:39:15,811
Let's say everything.

712
00:39:16,562 --> 00:39:17,646
Even the painful truths?

713
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:18,981
Especially the painful truths.

714
00:39:20,524 --> 00:39:24,320
We have to have a complete and honest
review about our relationship.

715
00:39:24,403 --> 00:39:25,780
That's what the road trip is for.

716
00:39:25,863 --> 00:39:27,698
Tuks, let's make an agreement.

717
00:39:28,616 --> 00:39:30,034
We will take a breakup trip.

718
00:39:31,911 --> 00:39:35,122
We'll survive through traffic,

719
00:39:35,873 --> 00:39:36,832
tears,

720
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:38,542
and the truth.

721
00:39:40,252 --> 00:39:41,170
Deal?

722
00:39:42,046 --> 00:39:43,631
That sounds so corporate.

723
00:39:43,714 --> 00:39:44,965
Let's call it a promise.

724
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:47,843
No, better than a promise.

725
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:48,803
Mm?

726
00:39:48,886 --> 00:39:50,179
A covenant.

727
00:40:05,403 --> 00:40:08,697
My gosh! That should've been the ending!

728
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:10,991
We should've gotten married after that.

729
00:40:19,875 --> 00:40:22,169
Okay, double time.
Frame one, okay?

730
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:23,838
Let's lock the shot
before the director gets here.

731
00:40:23,921 --> 00:40:26,090
Tina! Costume. Wardrobe.

732
00:40:26,173 --> 00:40:28,843
Miss Giuliarose!
This is the way to makeup.

733
00:40:28,926 --> 00:40:31,512
There's no need. I'm ready to shoot.
Where's the director?

734
00:40:31,595 --> 00:40:32,471
He's on his way.

735
00:40:32,555 --> 00:40:34,181
Let's say hi to the Dolce Bravo team.

736
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:35,516
Tuks, where are you?

737
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:37,268
Tuks, we're still on the road.

738
00:40:38,853 --> 00:40:40,646
The client pitch ran overtime.

739
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:44,733
Giuliarose and the clients are here.

740
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:47,903
The traffic hasn't moved for hours.
What do you want me to do?

741
00:40:47,987 --> 00:40:49,572
Can't we reschedule?

742
00:40:49,655 --> 00:40:53,451
Giuliarose is flying to Paris tomorrow.
She'll be there for two months.

743
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,870
When is the release date?

744
00:40:56,745 --> 00:40:58,080
End of this month.

745
00:40:58,581 --> 00:41:00,916
Shit! This is bad!

746
00:41:01,709 --> 00:41:03,627
Can you wait for me, Tuks?

747
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:07,506
We only have two hours until sunset, Tuks.

748
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:10,885
Shoot it.

749
00:41:10,968 --> 00:41:12,636
No.

750
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:14,013
I'll call Shane.

751
00:41:14,096 --> 00:41:16,682
No. I'd rather have you
direct this thing than Shane.

752
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:20,352
Cisco.

753
00:41:20,436 --> 00:41:22,897
I don't know what to do.

754
00:41:22,980 --> 00:41:24,732
I'm getting bored.

755
00:41:24,815 --> 00:41:27,026
We're running out of daylight.

756
00:41:27,109 --> 00:41:29,904
Tukie, just follow my storyboard.

757
00:41:29,987 --> 00:41:32,239
Everything's written there.
It's going to be okay.

758
00:41:32,323 --> 00:41:33,657
You can do it.

759
00:41:33,741 --> 00:41:34,658
Okay?

760
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:37,578
Oh my god.

761
00:41:43,751 --> 00:41:45,419
<i></i>Preview!

762
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:47,630
She doesn't look happy
with the product.

763
00:41:47,713 --> 00:41:49,757
Is she going through something?

764
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,718
- Does she have a problem?
- That's not my problem.

765
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:55,304
Giuliarose is throwing a fit again.

766
00:41:55,387 --> 00:41:57,056
We've been here all day.
How many more shots to go?

767
00:41:57,139 --> 00:41:58,557
Poor Cheska. How will she finish this?

768
00:41:58,641 --> 00:42:01,310
Following Cisco's storyboard,
two more shots to go.

769
00:42:01,393 --> 00:42:02,728
- What should we do?
- Here.

770
00:42:03,312 --> 00:42:05,314
Kookai, Vince, follow me.

771
00:42:05,397 --> 00:42:06,232
Stand by.

772
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:08,234
Okay, guys, I'm here!

773
00:42:09,026 --> 00:42:10,402
Stay here, we're rolling.

774
00:42:11,487 --> 00:42:13,280
- Which shot is this?
- Here's the storyboard.

775
00:42:13,364 --> 00:42:14,240
I don't know.

776
00:42:14,323 --> 00:42:16,367
- Let's see what Cheska's doing.
- You don't know?

777
00:42:16,450 --> 00:42:17,618
Quiet.

778
00:42:18,744 --> 00:42:20,538
Okay, let's wait.

779
00:42:20,621 --> 00:42:22,373
Are you okay?

780
00:42:22,456 --> 00:42:24,583
I'm okay.

781
00:42:25,584 --> 00:42:26,835
Do you want to talk?

782
00:42:30,297 --> 00:42:32,049
Be quiet. She's comforting her.

783
00:42:32,132 --> 00:42:33,259
Tissue.

784
00:42:35,177 --> 00:42:36,595
I'm sorry.

785
00:42:36,679 --> 00:42:37,888
Roll the camera.

786
00:42:52,027 --> 00:42:52,903
Cheska, here.

787
00:42:54,613 --> 00:42:56,073
To make you happy.

788
00:42:56,740 --> 00:42:59,952
- Oh, she's finally smiling!
- Yeah!

789
00:43:00,035 --> 00:43:03,205
Oh my God.
That's what Cheska's been doing.

790
00:43:03,289 --> 00:43:04,415
Now I get it.

791
00:43:04,498 --> 00:43:08,294
Cheska's directing style works.

792
00:43:08,377 --> 00:43:09,295
Cut!

793
00:43:09,378 --> 00:43:10,754
We got it!

794
00:43:10,838 --> 00:43:12,548
That's the shot!

795
00:43:12,631 --> 00:43:14,425
Cheska, thank you.

796
00:43:14,508 --> 00:43:15,384
I love it.

797
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:16,302
Thank you.

798
00:43:19,430 --> 00:43:22,516
From now on,
I want her to always be my director.

799
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:25,269
Cheska is amazing!

800
00:43:25,811 --> 00:43:26,812
Thank you.

801
00:43:30,566 --> 00:43:32,318
Thank you.

802
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:35,070
- Best director!
- Not really.

803
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:37,990
No, really.
I'll even recommend you to my friends.

804
00:43:38,073 --> 00:43:39,033
Hey, Allie!

805
00:43:39,116 --> 00:43:42,369
Can we request that
Cheska direct my upcoming projects?

806
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:43,954
So Cisco won't be directing anymore?

807
00:43:44,038 --> 00:43:47,833
- I don't think so.
- Cheska is really great.

808
00:44:24,119 --> 00:44:25,579
I love you.

809
00:44:37,091 --> 00:44:38,717
I love you more.

810
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:43,681
Hi, Grandpa!

811
00:44:43,764 --> 00:44:46,767
Congrats on the
Dolce Bravo ad, Cheska!

812
00:44:46,850 --> 00:44:48,477
- Thank you!
- Yes, Cheska.

813
00:44:48,560 --> 00:44:52,981
You know, I never really liked Giuliarose,
but now she seems so real and relatable.

814
00:44:53,065 --> 00:44:54,525
- Right?
- Exactly.

815
00:44:54,608 --> 00:44:56,610
I've always had a crush on Giulia

816
00:44:56,693 --> 00:44:58,445
and now I want to comfort her.

817
00:44:58,529 --> 00:45:01,949
Ew. That's not what we're talking about!

818
00:45:02,032 --> 00:45:05,702
It was so good,
even my friends shared the ad.

819
00:45:05,786 --> 00:45:09,415
You know, Cheska,
I told my friends you directed it,

820
00:45:09,498 --> 00:45:11,708
and they're so excited
to see your future work.

821
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:15,587
Thank you, but the birthday boy
should get all the credit.

822
00:45:15,671 --> 00:45:16,797
- Really?
- That was his idea.

823
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:17,965
- Wow!
- I just executed it.

824
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:20,342
That's nice, Cisco.

825
00:45:20,926 --> 00:45:22,302
Good job, son.

826
00:45:24,179 --> 00:45:26,348
How long will you be doing that, Cisco?

827
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:30,394
Grandpa?

828
00:45:30,477 --> 00:45:32,146
You've been at it for a while now.

829
00:45:33,147 --> 00:45:36,358
Cheska already beat you to a big hit.

830
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:39,361
Dad, Cisco's done a lot already--

831
00:45:39,445 --> 00:45:40,404
Small,

832
00:45:41,238 --> 00:45:42,906
inconsequential stuff.

833
00:45:44,575 --> 00:45:46,243
Not as viral as Cheska's.

834
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:48,787
Perhaps

835
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:51,999
you need to reconsider
your career plans, Cisco.

836
00:45:52,082 --> 00:45:53,917
- Pa.
- Look.

837
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:56,712
We need a Marketing and Advertising Head

838
00:45:56,795 --> 00:45:58,672
in the Logistics Division.

839
00:45:59,798 --> 00:46:01,300
Why don't you join us, Cisco?

840
00:46:03,802 --> 00:46:07,681
Grandpa, I have no plans
of entering the family business.

841
00:46:08,974 --> 00:46:11,310
That's what your papa said too.

842
00:46:11,393 --> 00:46:14,021
Until reality hit him.

843
00:46:15,731 --> 00:46:19,985
Not everyone can make
their passion their career.

844
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:22,196
What do you want, son?

845
00:46:22,821 --> 00:46:26,783
Do you want to grow old
with nothing to show for?

846
00:46:28,202 --> 00:46:30,454
You might get left behind.

847
00:46:30,537 --> 00:46:32,372
Even by your siblings.

848
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:34,291
You are being silly, Grandpa.

849
00:46:34,374 --> 00:46:37,211
Look, what I'm saying is,

850
00:46:38,337 --> 00:46:40,214
in a creative industry,

851
00:46:41,131 --> 00:46:42,883
passion is not enough.

852
00:46:44,092 --> 00:46:45,969
Hell, hard work is not enough.

853
00:46:46,970 --> 00:46:49,973
What you need is solid talent.

854
00:46:51,391 --> 00:46:55,229
If you're just middling,
or at best mediocre,

855
00:46:56,146 --> 00:46:59,316
you'll end up like your mother.

856
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:01,151
A has-been.

857
00:47:02,819 --> 00:47:06,073
Dad, let's just eat.
The food is good.

858
00:47:06,156 --> 00:47:07,449
Let's just enjoy it.

859
00:47:07,533 --> 00:47:08,909
Right.

860
00:47:11,245 --> 00:47:12,996
We have to break through
the social media space.

861
00:47:13,080 --> 00:47:14,289
Sir, the clients are here.

862
00:47:14,373 --> 00:47:15,499
Let's go.

863
00:47:15,582 --> 00:47:18,293
I heard Sir Shane is resigning.

864
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:20,796
Girl, no! He just got transferred
to the other wing.

865
00:47:20,879 --> 00:47:21,755
Why?

866
00:47:21,838 --> 00:47:25,551
He's now a junior member of the board

867
00:47:25,634 --> 00:47:27,094
as the new head of G Spot.

868
00:47:27,177 --> 00:47:29,763
Wow! He's a big boss now.

869
00:47:30,472 --> 00:47:32,808
We're presenting the brand as aspirational

870
00:47:32,891 --> 00:47:34,476
and still accessible!

871
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:36,687
So the tone is confident.

872
00:47:36,770 --> 00:47:37,854
Slightly irreverent.

873
00:47:37,938 --> 00:47:40,399
But that's not for our target market.

874
00:47:40,482 --> 00:47:42,359
But that's the type of tone you need.

875
00:47:42,442 --> 00:47:44,945
We need to break through
the social media space.

876
00:47:45,654 --> 00:47:47,322
Your brand's already
falling behind!

877
00:47:49,157 --> 00:47:51,868
You know why?
You present yourself as super safe.

878
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:54,037
So forgettable.

879
00:47:55,038 --> 00:47:57,833
Do you want our business or not?

880
00:47:59,042 --> 00:48:00,544
Do you want me or not?

881
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:03,755
Because we're telling you
what you need to hear,

882
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:05,716
not what you want to hear.

883
00:48:06,717 --> 00:48:07,926
It's your choice.

884
00:48:09,428 --> 00:48:13,682
Rommel, can you give Cisco and I a second?

885
00:48:13,765 --> 00:48:18,020
We just have an urgent client concern
for another brand.

886
00:48:18,103 --> 00:48:20,439
Cheska, can you continue…

887
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:22,649
…presenting the campaign to Mr. Reyes?

888
00:48:23,275 --> 00:48:24,359
Yes, Mr. G.

889
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:29,156
- What was that?
- Sir, you have to understand.

890
00:48:29,239 --> 00:48:31,450
- I was just being honest with them.
- No, you were being rude!

891
00:48:31,533 --> 00:48:33,827
That's my way of making sure
that there's a strategy in place--

892
00:48:33,910 --> 00:48:36,455
You don't call insulting
your clients strategy!

893
00:48:36,538 --> 00:48:38,790
Strategy does not work

894
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:41,168
if they don't want to work with you.

895
00:48:44,296 --> 00:48:45,422
Take a break.

896
00:48:46,048 --> 00:48:47,966
Sir, I'm not taking a break.
This is my account.

897
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:49,092
No!

898
00:48:51,553 --> 00:48:53,221
Take a break.

899
00:48:55,349 --> 00:48:57,059
We will handle this from here.

900
00:49:08,278 --> 00:49:09,488
- Great!
- Nice!

901
00:49:09,571 --> 00:49:10,572
Thank you for the trust.

902
00:49:10,656 --> 00:49:12,699
Well, we love Cheska's vision
for the company.

903
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:14,159
That's why we're sticking with you.

904
00:49:14,242 --> 00:49:16,828
And we promise to deliver
within the timeframe.

905
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:17,746
Great!

906
00:49:17,829 --> 00:49:20,582
But we want Cheska to lead the campaign.

907
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:21,667
Right, Cheska?

908
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:22,876
Of course!

909
00:49:22,959 --> 00:49:23,919
Cheska it is.

910
00:49:24,002 --> 00:49:26,213
- Thank you, Cheska.
- Thank you so much.

911
00:49:26,296 --> 00:49:28,715
Thank you, sir. Thank you.

912
00:49:28,799 --> 00:49:31,551
- Sir, I'll just accompany them downstairs.
- All right, see you!

913
00:49:34,596 --> 00:49:36,181
As the new head of G Spot,

914
00:49:36,264 --> 00:49:41,019
Shane will handle all planning, budgeting,
and staffing decisions,

915
00:49:41,603 --> 00:49:46,483
while you can focus on
developing venture accounts.

916
00:49:46,566 --> 00:49:53,073
Smaller emerging brands
open to partnership models.

917
00:49:53,699 --> 00:49:58,078
Cheska will now be
reporting directly to Shane.

918
00:49:59,413 --> 00:50:01,581
She'll be
on developmental assignment.

919
00:50:01,665 --> 00:50:04,710
And I'll be training her on account
and strategic management.

920
00:50:05,419 --> 00:50:06,962
You'll still be doing local accounts,

921
00:50:07,045 --> 00:50:10,465
but we're really positioning her
to bring in international clients.

922
00:50:11,425 --> 00:50:12,342
Why?

923
00:50:13,385 --> 00:50:15,220
I can bring in international clients.

924
00:50:15,804 --> 00:50:17,055
Oh really?

925
00:50:18,014 --> 00:50:20,225
You've always had contact
with an international account,

926
00:50:20,308 --> 00:50:23,729
but why haven't you offered
our services to them?

927
00:50:28,900 --> 00:50:31,570
We found out from Cheska

928
00:50:31,653 --> 00:50:37,284
that your stepdad
is the CEO of Taylor-Smith Australia.

929
00:50:37,367 --> 00:50:39,244
You want me to pull the nepo baby card?

930
00:50:39,953 --> 00:50:41,663
But this is business.

931
00:50:41,747 --> 00:50:43,248
Easy for you to say.

932
00:50:43,957 --> 00:50:48,086
Cisco, we all want what's best
for the company.

933
00:50:48,170 --> 00:50:49,129
For G Spot!

934
00:50:49,212 --> 00:50:51,339
For us to stay competitive.

935
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:54,217
- And adapt to a very volatile--
- Stay competitive?

936
00:50:54,760 --> 00:50:55,844
Adapting?

937
00:50:56,803 --> 00:50:59,139
While keeping me on the sidelines?

938
00:51:01,683 --> 00:51:03,518
Sir, I built this division.

939
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:05,896
I even named it!

940
00:51:05,979 --> 00:51:09,024
And now I'm being asked to chase startups

941
00:51:09,107 --> 00:51:10,692
while someone else heads this division

942
00:51:10,776 --> 00:51:14,237
and my subordinate
trains to take over my job!

943
00:51:15,071 --> 00:51:16,948
We are just restructuring.

944
00:51:17,032 --> 00:51:18,116
Realigning roles--

945
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:19,326
You're pushing me away.

946
00:51:19,951 --> 00:51:21,578
You don't want me here.

947
00:51:23,079 --> 00:51:24,664
That's not what we're saying.

948
00:51:26,333 --> 00:51:27,417
It's okay.

949
00:51:28,001 --> 00:51:29,169
I get it.

950
00:51:32,923 --> 00:51:33,924
I'm out.

951
00:51:39,721 --> 00:51:40,931
The logo is okay.

952
00:51:41,014 --> 00:51:44,017
- We just need to make it bolder.
- Right.

953
00:51:44,100 --> 00:51:46,144
Hey! What do you mean bold?

954
00:51:46,228 --> 00:51:48,313
I've changed my mind!
I'm pulling my money out!

955
00:51:48,396 --> 00:51:51,274
- Hey, don't, JC!
- Please don't!

956
00:51:51,358 --> 00:51:52,984
How about colors?
Should we do all black?

957
00:51:53,068 --> 00:51:55,111
Why not?
As long as it's timeless.

958
00:51:55,195 --> 00:51:56,613
Do you want to try a 3D printer?

959
00:51:56,696 --> 00:51:58,949
- I'll add some bevel and texture.
- Sounds great!

960
00:51:59,032 --> 00:52:00,116
Hello.

961
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:01,576
- Tuks?
- There she is!

962
00:52:01,660 --> 00:52:02,911
Finally!

963
00:52:02,994 --> 00:52:04,955
You're home!

964
00:52:05,539 --> 00:52:08,708
Shawn, Tuks, our graphic designer.

965
00:52:08,792 --> 00:52:11,169
Mookie's friend.
And my buddy from college.

966
00:52:11,253 --> 00:52:12,087
- Hey.
- Hi.

967
00:52:12,170 --> 00:52:14,214
So nice to finally meet you.

968
00:52:14,297 --> 00:52:15,966
I'm the old Cheska.

969
00:52:16,591 --> 00:52:18,134
Did you guys smooch too?

970
00:52:18,218 --> 00:52:19,845
JC!

971
00:52:19,928 --> 00:52:21,346
Of course not!

972
00:52:21,429 --> 00:52:24,850
I was his producer
in all our college projects.

973
00:52:24,933 --> 00:52:26,434
I heard you're his new Mookie.

974
00:52:26,518 --> 00:52:28,562
Female version, of course.

975
00:52:29,145 --> 00:52:32,065
Upgraded version actually!

976
00:52:32,148 --> 00:52:36,403
Mookie will make sure the operations
are set so we can launch soon.

977
00:52:36,486 --> 00:52:37,487
Launch?

978
00:52:37,571 --> 00:52:39,030
What launch, Tuks?

979
00:52:39,114 --> 00:52:41,116
That's the surprise, Tuks!

980
00:52:41,199 --> 00:52:44,202
JC finally said yes!
He's going to be one of our investors.

981
00:52:44,286 --> 00:52:46,788
I sold my kidneys so I could invest.

982
00:52:46,872 --> 00:52:47,873
You're the best, JC!

983
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:50,458
Bonj is also investing!

984
00:52:50,542 --> 00:52:52,294
- That's why he was asking me--
- Woo!

985
00:52:52,377 --> 00:52:54,296
Cisco!

986
00:52:54,379 --> 00:52:55,338
Sorry, sorry.

987
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:57,257
I'm okay! Don't worry, guys.

988
00:52:57,340 --> 00:52:58,758
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

989
00:52:58,842 --> 00:53:01,052
You've had a bit too much to drink, Cisco.

990
00:53:01,136 --> 00:53:02,304
Spill on aisle three.

991
00:53:02,387 --> 00:53:04,055
You're good, you're good.

992
00:53:04,139 --> 00:53:05,974
As I was saying, Tuks,

993
00:53:06,057 --> 00:53:09,311
since I'm no longer a corporate slave,

994
00:53:09,394 --> 00:53:11,855
why do we need bosses

995
00:53:11,938 --> 00:53:14,107
if we can be our own boss?

996
00:53:14,190 --> 00:53:15,275
Huh?

997
00:53:16,526 --> 00:53:20,447
I mean, since we always
work best together,

998
00:53:21,281 --> 00:53:23,074
why do it for someone else

999
00:53:23,158 --> 00:53:25,076
if we can do it for ourselves?

1000
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:26,244
Together?

1001
00:53:27,245 --> 00:53:28,330
You and me!

1002
00:53:28,914 --> 00:53:30,957
Let's start our own production house!

1003
00:53:31,666 --> 00:53:35,211
And the best part?
Cisco already has a name.

1004
00:53:36,504 --> 00:53:38,840
Tuks! CXC!

1005
00:53:39,424 --> 00:53:41,468
Cisco and Cheska!

1006
00:53:41,551 --> 00:53:44,012
It's great, right?

1007
00:53:44,095 --> 00:53:45,347
Not bad.

1008
00:53:45,430 --> 00:53:47,641
You'll join me here, won't you?

1009
00:53:48,224 --> 00:53:49,225
Right?

1010
00:53:49,768 --> 00:53:52,103
There's no CXC without Cheska.

1011
00:53:55,315 --> 00:53:57,609
Only if you want to, of course.

1012
00:53:57,692 --> 00:53:59,986
We only need
one last big investor.

1013
00:54:00,070 --> 00:54:02,530
Where are we going
to find another investor?

1014
00:54:03,156 --> 00:54:05,533
- Desperate times, desperate measures.
- Why not your dad?

1015
00:54:05,617 --> 00:54:06,660
Your grandpa?

1016
00:54:06,743 --> 00:54:07,827
Can't they invest?

1017
00:54:09,287 --> 00:54:10,246
Ches…

1018
00:54:10,330 --> 00:54:11,706
Are you really resigning?

1019
00:54:20,507 --> 00:54:21,508
Dad.

1020
00:54:22,759 --> 00:54:25,136
I already agreed to invest.

1021
00:54:26,429 --> 00:54:27,889
Let us help Cisco.

1022
00:54:28,765 --> 00:54:31,643
Your grandson rarely asks for our help.

1023
00:54:33,645 --> 00:54:35,563
Why are you the one begging?

1024
00:54:37,232 --> 00:54:39,442
Is your son too arrogant to beg?

1025
00:54:47,242 --> 00:54:48,451
Please, Grandpa.

1026
00:54:49,077 --> 00:54:50,453
Please what?

1027
00:55:05,135 --> 00:55:06,803
Help me build my business.

1028
00:55:07,637 --> 00:55:08,722
I need your help.

1029
00:55:10,473 --> 00:55:12,183
Is Cheska part of this?

1030
00:55:12,267 --> 00:55:13,226
Yes.

1031
00:55:14,352 --> 00:55:15,729
She is?

1032
00:55:17,105 --> 00:55:18,440
She believes in this?

1033
00:55:19,190 --> 00:55:20,358
Enough to leave Guinto Group?

1034
00:55:20,442 --> 00:55:23,194
She will oversee operations
and client management.

1035
00:55:30,243 --> 00:55:31,119
Good.

1036
00:55:32,287 --> 00:55:33,496
Good.

1037
00:55:34,789 --> 00:55:36,624
Kiko, call Albert.

1038
00:55:36,708 --> 00:55:39,294
Tell him to prepare a check for Cisco.

1039
00:55:40,045 --> 00:55:41,171
Yes, Dad.

1040
00:55:45,008 --> 00:55:46,092
Thank you, Grandpa.

1041
00:55:46,926 --> 00:55:48,595
I will not let you down.

1042
00:55:49,804 --> 00:55:50,972
I promise.

1043
00:55:54,142 --> 00:55:56,144
Thank you, Grandpa.

1044
00:55:56,227 --> 00:55:57,270
Thank you.

1045
00:56:02,150 --> 00:56:03,651
Wow.

1046
00:56:03,735 --> 00:56:05,278
- It's spacious!
- It's perfect.

1047
00:56:05,361 --> 00:56:08,114
- Cool, isn't it?
- Looks even better in person.

1048
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:10,408
This can be our statement wall.

1049
00:56:10,492 --> 00:56:13,286
We can have our centerpiece over here.

1050
00:56:13,369 --> 00:56:15,789
I can paint it!

1051
00:56:15,872 --> 00:56:17,207
How much?

1052
00:56:17,290 --> 00:56:18,291
Do it for free.

1053
00:56:18,374 --> 00:56:19,417
Part of your investment.

1054
00:56:19,501 --> 00:56:20,877
- For free?
- Mooks!

1055
00:56:20,960 --> 00:56:24,714
- Content corner, what do you think?
- Editing bays here would be better.

1056
00:56:24,798 --> 00:56:28,468
- The content corner can be there instead.
- What do you think, Shawn?

1057
00:56:28,551 --> 00:56:30,720
- Yeah!
- This spot has better lighting.

1058
00:56:30,804 --> 00:56:34,390
Wow! What a glow-up!

1059
00:56:35,016 --> 00:56:38,061
She's so ready to be a CEO!

1060
00:56:39,479 --> 00:56:40,897
You look…

1061
00:56:44,359 --> 00:56:45,568
different.

1062
00:56:48,404 --> 00:56:49,656
I just…

1063
00:56:52,117 --> 00:56:53,660
needed a change.

1064
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:58,373
That's exactly what you're gonna get!
Welcome to our new content playground!

1065
00:56:58,456 --> 00:57:00,708
We'll provide groundbreaking
content creation.

1066
00:57:00,792 --> 00:57:01,960
What do you think?

1067
00:57:02,043 --> 00:57:04,838
Mookie! Did you get our equipment already?

1068
00:57:04,921 --> 00:57:06,005
We still need more.

1069
00:57:06,089 --> 00:57:08,967
We'll secure more
once we receive the funding.

1070
00:57:09,050 --> 00:57:11,386
I'll get a check from Grandpa later.

1071
00:57:11,469 --> 00:57:15,014
- So we can prepare for the soft launch!
- Cisco--

1072
00:57:15,098 --> 00:57:17,100
- Nice!
- Cisco.

1073
00:57:17,183 --> 00:57:18,059
Cisco.

1074
00:57:18,977 --> 00:57:20,228
Can we talk?

1075
00:57:21,062 --> 00:57:23,022
Yes. Later.

1076
00:57:23,648 --> 00:57:28,111
You know, I'm excited to see
the Cisco and Cheska chemistry!

1077
00:57:28,194 --> 00:57:30,488
Oh, you boys have not seen
our chemistry together.

1078
00:57:30,572 --> 00:57:31,823
We make magic.

1079
00:57:32,449 --> 00:57:35,076
- For sure.
- They're like chemists, actually!

1080
00:57:35,160 --> 00:57:36,453
Cisco!

1081
00:57:42,333 --> 00:57:43,960
I'm not resigning.

1082
00:57:46,671 --> 00:57:47,755
I'm sorry.

1083
00:57:47,839 --> 00:57:49,466
I'm not joining you.

1084
00:58:04,439 --> 00:58:05,356
Hey!

1085
00:58:05,440 --> 00:58:06,524
Cisco!

1086
00:58:06,608 --> 00:58:08,193
Long time, no see.

1087
00:58:08,735 --> 00:58:10,570
I like your new hair.

1088
00:58:11,654 --> 00:58:12,447
I need gas.

1089
00:58:12,530 --> 00:58:13,531
Oh.

1090
00:58:13,615 --> 00:58:15,617
That's been out of business
for a while now.

1091
00:58:15,700 --> 00:58:19,078
Even the eatery is closing down soon.

1092
00:58:19,662 --> 00:58:20,497
Really?

1093
00:58:20,580 --> 00:58:23,416
Yup, it went bankrupt.

1094
00:58:37,388 --> 00:58:38,598
See?

1095
00:58:39,265 --> 00:58:41,976
Even this place is trying
to move on from you.

1096
00:58:42,060 --> 00:58:44,938
Everything must end.
Why can't you accept that?

1097
00:58:45,021 --> 00:58:47,941
Everyone has moved on except you.

1098
00:58:48,024 --> 00:58:50,151
I need to say sorry to you.

1099
00:58:51,778 --> 00:58:53,613
I still need to make it up to you.

1100
00:58:54,822 --> 00:58:56,741
Cisco, I'm not coming back!

1101
00:58:56,824 --> 00:58:57,909
Don't say that.

1102
00:58:58,409 --> 00:58:59,452
Don't say that!

1103
00:58:59,536 --> 00:59:01,204
Why don't you believe me?

1104
00:59:01,287 --> 00:59:04,707
Because the thought of you coming back
is the only thing keeping me alive!

1105
00:59:06,334 --> 00:59:08,253
Because if it's just me, I'm done.

1106
00:59:09,837 --> 00:59:12,215
I hate myself for being alive!

1107
00:59:33,861 --> 00:59:36,281
If my driver answers.

1108
00:59:36,364 --> 00:59:40,201
- He doesn't speak Japanese.
- I told you so.

1109
00:59:40,285 --> 00:59:42,203
Let's just bring your car, Shane.

1110
00:59:48,001 --> 00:59:51,337
Let's eat already because I'm so hungry!

1111
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:52,797
- Ma'am, your bag.
- Thanks, Nabi!

1112
00:59:52,880 --> 00:59:54,382
- Let me--
- I got it.

1113
00:59:55,133 --> 00:59:56,509
Cisco, are you joining us for dinner?

1114
00:59:57,343 --> 00:59:58,177
Huh?

1115
00:59:58,261 --> 00:59:59,971
Tuks, I messaged you…

1116
01:00:02,098 --> 01:00:03,516
I didn't receive anything.

1117
01:00:04,309 --> 01:00:05,685
It's okay, Cheska.

1118
01:00:05,768 --> 01:00:07,729
We can have dinner some other time.

1119
01:00:08,813 --> 01:00:10,565
- Sorry, Mr. G.
- It's okay.

1120
01:00:10,648 --> 01:00:11,524
Cisco.

1121
01:00:12,692 --> 01:00:14,235
Nice seeing you again, Cisco.

1122
01:00:15,278 --> 01:00:16,988
Oh, Cheska, congrats again.

1123
01:00:17,071 --> 01:00:18,072
You deserve it.

1124
01:00:31,586 --> 01:00:32,712
They gave you my job.

1125
01:00:35,548 --> 01:00:36,674
Damn it!

1126
01:00:39,052 --> 01:00:40,345
They gave you my position.

1127
01:00:45,808 --> 01:00:48,770
You know this is their strategy, right?
For the upcoming client pitch.

1128
01:00:48,853 --> 01:00:50,104
You against me?

1129
01:00:51,105 --> 01:00:52,106
What a smart move, huh?

1130
01:00:52,190 --> 01:00:55,193
They waited for me to leave
before they promoted you.

1131
01:00:55,818 --> 01:00:58,363
It's probably because Shane likes you.

1132
01:00:58,446 --> 01:00:59,614
Now that's foul.

1133
01:00:59,697 --> 01:01:01,115
Am I wrong?

1134
01:01:01,199 --> 01:01:03,368
He's always had a thing for you.

1135
01:01:04,285 --> 01:01:05,536
But I got you.

1136
01:01:06,329 --> 01:01:07,789
Can't admit that?

1137
01:01:07,872 --> 01:01:09,582
Just admit this then.

1138
01:01:09,666 --> 01:01:14,754
That fucking promotion is the only reason
why you won't join me in CXC.

1139
01:01:14,837 --> 01:01:16,673
You used your family as an excuse!

1140
01:01:16,756 --> 01:01:18,800
You know my family is in a lot of debt--

1141
01:01:18,883 --> 01:01:21,260
Exactly! CXC would have
been the best option!

1142
01:01:21,344 --> 01:01:23,513
- For your financial needs!
- My brother is having a kid!

1143
01:01:23,596 --> 01:01:26,599
- This is your own company--
- My parents rely on me.

1144
01:01:26,683 --> 01:01:28,184
You could earn more here!

1145
01:01:28,267 --> 01:01:29,394
In the future!

1146
01:01:29,477 --> 01:01:32,021
But right now,
I need a stable job, Cisco--

1147
01:01:32,105 --> 01:01:34,107
Just tell me you don't trust me, Cheska.

1148
01:01:34,190 --> 01:01:36,067
- What?
- You don't trust me.

1149
01:01:36,150 --> 01:01:38,861
You don't trust that I can succeed.
That this company will make money.

1150
01:01:38,945 --> 01:01:40,947
- Cisco, I believe in you--
- Really?

1151
01:01:41,030 --> 01:01:42,323
That I can make this work?

1152
01:01:42,407 --> 01:01:45,702
- That I can provide for you, Cheska?
- Cisco, it's not about trust!

1153
01:01:45,785 --> 01:01:47,912
It's about responsibility!

1154
01:01:47,995 --> 01:01:51,082
So now I'm irresponsible? Me?!

1155
01:01:51,165 --> 01:01:55,169
It's about my, <i>my,</i> responsibilities!

1156
01:01:55,712 --> 01:01:58,506
It's easy for you to quit
and start your own business

1157
01:01:58,589 --> 01:02:00,758
because no one is relying on you!

1158
01:02:00,842 --> 01:02:03,886
You can ask for help from your family.
My life is different from yours.

1159
01:02:03,970 --> 01:02:06,055
Then you shouldn't have led me on!

1160
01:02:06,139 --> 01:02:07,140
Led you on?

1161
01:02:07,223 --> 01:02:10,518
I thought we were building
CXC together, Cheska!

1162
01:02:11,436 --> 01:02:12,937
I thought you were on my side.

1163
01:02:13,020 --> 01:02:14,731
I am!

1164
01:02:14,814 --> 01:02:19,277
But that doesn't mean
I'll do everything you say!

1165
01:02:23,322 --> 01:02:24,741
So you're not leaving Mr. G?

1166
01:02:26,325 --> 01:02:28,286
I can't right now.

1167
01:02:28,369 --> 01:02:29,412
Right now?

1168
01:02:30,663 --> 01:02:31,706
Or ever?

1169
01:02:33,666 --> 01:02:36,294
So you'll only join me
once the business is successful?

1170
01:02:36,836 --> 01:02:38,755
Once I've proven myself?

1171
01:02:41,674 --> 01:02:43,968
I thought I didn't have to
prove myself to you.

1172
01:02:56,522 --> 01:02:57,899
What are you doing?

1173
01:02:57,982 --> 01:03:00,610
I just hope you realize
what this means, Cheska.

1174
01:03:03,154 --> 01:03:07,033
You were promoted
because they want to pit you against me.

1175
01:03:07,116 --> 01:03:09,118
This has been Mr. G
and Shane's plan all along.

1176
01:03:09,202 --> 01:03:10,369
I hope you know.

1177
01:03:11,913 --> 01:03:12,997
But fine.

1178
01:03:15,500 --> 01:03:16,959
Let's keep this professional.

1179
01:03:19,796 --> 01:03:21,005
I'll see you at the pitch.

1180
01:03:43,236 --> 01:03:45,988
Here's the thing you asked me to buy.

1181
01:03:46,072 --> 01:03:47,365
- Shawn?
- Yes?

1182
01:03:47,448 --> 01:03:49,784
- Why is it so small?
- It's all they had.

1183
01:03:49,867 --> 01:03:51,369
Start small!

1184
01:03:51,452 --> 01:03:54,163
<i>Whatever idea we will pitch</i>
<i>to Nuevas Alturas,</i>

1185
01:03:54,247 --> 01:03:55,873
<i>they can't just imagine it.</i>

1186
01:03:57,124 --> 01:03:58,501
We have to have proof!

1187
01:04:00,461 --> 01:04:01,379
Guys!

1188
01:04:05,591 --> 01:04:11,681
It needs to be shot
and edited already for our tech.

1189
01:04:11,764 --> 01:04:14,892
- Do you understand what he's saying?
- Nope.

1190
01:04:14,976 --> 01:04:16,727
We need a live demo.

1191
01:04:16,811 --> 01:04:21,774
The initial market scan said
condo ownership is a low priority.

1192
01:04:21,858 --> 01:04:23,568
There's also an emotional barrier.

1193
01:04:23,651 --> 01:04:26,529
They don't see the Nuevas Alturas condo
as something they deserve.

1194
01:04:26,612 --> 01:04:30,408
And we deserve a confident
diva queen leader!

1195
01:04:30,491 --> 01:04:33,286
Drink medicine if you have a headache.

1196
01:04:33,369 --> 01:04:37,874
Otherwise, enough being
a martyr girlfriend.

1197
01:04:37,957 --> 01:04:38,916
Mm?

1198
01:04:39,500 --> 01:04:42,753
Go on. Have a reset.

1199
01:05:12,700 --> 01:05:13,701
G?

1200
01:05:16,787 --> 01:05:17,914
Spot.

1201
01:05:17,997 --> 01:05:19,624
Let's go!

1202
01:05:19,707 --> 01:05:22,585
G Spot will make the same promises we can.

1203
01:05:22,668 --> 01:05:23,544
Agility.

1204
01:05:23,628 --> 01:05:24,962
Affordability.

1205
01:05:25,630 --> 01:05:28,841
They'll use the credentials
of Guinto Group.

1206
01:05:28,925 --> 01:05:33,054
So we leverage with conviction,
not just credentials.

1207
01:05:33,137 --> 01:05:36,807
Oh my! We're convicted!
There's no escape!

1208
01:05:36,891 --> 01:05:38,559
We're just investors here, right?

1209
01:05:38,643 --> 01:05:39,852
Guys, guys!

1210
01:05:40,478 --> 01:05:42,313
G Spot will keep things simple.

1211
01:05:43,189 --> 01:05:45,358
We'll make simple look small.

1212
01:05:45,441 --> 01:05:47,818
Other agencies will go for grand ideas

1213
01:05:47,902 --> 01:05:50,655
to match the high-end image of the client.

1214
01:05:50,738 --> 01:05:53,449
G Spot will go simple.

1215
01:05:53,532 --> 01:05:55,076
But not simplistic.

1216
01:05:55,159 --> 01:05:57,411
As a young person,

1217
01:05:57,495 --> 01:06:00,289
what does it mean
when you have your own condo?

1218
01:06:00,373 --> 01:06:02,124
It means I'm making money!

1219
01:06:02,208 --> 01:06:06,504
- You're not young!
- It means you're successful!

1220
01:06:06,587 --> 01:06:07,964
Yes, and…?

1221
01:06:08,047 --> 01:06:09,382
Your own world.

1222
01:06:09,465 --> 01:06:10,841
- Control?
- Yes.

1223
01:06:10,925 --> 01:06:12,635
Independence.

1224
01:06:14,053 --> 01:06:17,139
Having your own place
means all your hard work has paid off.

1225
01:06:17,223 --> 01:06:18,849
It's your reward for being the best.

1226
01:06:19,892 --> 01:06:22,436
Guys! Mookie.

1227
01:06:22,520 --> 01:06:24,063
Food from Cheska.

1228
01:06:24,146 --> 01:06:27,149
Perfect! My kidney is sick
of all the junk food.

1229
01:06:27,233 --> 01:06:28,275
Break time?

1230
01:06:28,359 --> 01:06:29,944
- Want some?
- No, thanks.

1231
01:06:30,027 --> 01:06:31,320
High-rise.

1232
01:06:31,404 --> 01:06:33,197
As you rise higher above everyone else.

1233
01:06:33,280 --> 01:06:34,657
Thoughts?

1234
01:06:34,740 --> 01:06:38,536
I don't like high-rise buildings
because it's lonely at the top.

1235
01:06:38,619 --> 01:06:39,704
Meaning?

1236
01:06:41,163 --> 01:06:42,540
Oh, rice porridge!

1237
01:06:42,623 --> 01:06:43,958
Hi, rice!

1238
01:06:44,041 --> 01:06:46,961
That's why it's important
that we're able to make choices

1239
01:06:47,044 --> 01:06:49,922
that we can stand by and commit to.

1240
01:06:50,006 --> 01:06:53,426
Choices that will help us grow
and change for the better.

1241
01:06:53,509 --> 01:06:56,887
CISCO DIDN'T EAT.

1242
01:06:56,971 --> 01:06:59,306
I told you so.

1243
01:07:01,517 --> 01:07:05,062
And if we get that right,
the condo sells itself!

1244
01:07:05,146 --> 01:07:08,065
And when you own
a Nuevas Alturas condominium,

1245
01:07:08,149 --> 01:07:09,984
you can finally say to the world,

1246
01:07:10,985 --> 01:07:12,028
"I've made it."

1247
01:07:12,111 --> 01:07:16,824
Where you can finally be yourself and say,

1248
01:07:16,907 --> 01:07:17,908
"I'm home."

1249
01:07:20,286 --> 01:07:21,454
You're ready!

1250
01:07:22,538 --> 01:07:23,497
Let's do this!

1251
01:07:23,581 --> 01:07:24,582
Cheers, guys!

1252
01:07:24,665 --> 01:07:26,167
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

1253
01:07:28,627 --> 01:07:30,171
They aren't home yet?

1254
01:07:30,254 --> 01:07:32,923
They work harder than we do.

1255
01:07:38,929 --> 01:07:40,097
Bonj!

1256
01:07:41,307 --> 01:07:43,976
I miss my bed!

1257
01:07:44,060 --> 01:07:47,146
- Come home already, I miss you!
- <i>I haven't slept yet.</i>

1258
01:07:47,229 --> 01:07:48,773
Bonj, how's Cisco?

1259
01:07:49,398 --> 01:07:52,234
Bonj! Confidentiality.

1260
01:07:52,318 --> 01:07:54,528
- All right, bye.
- That's why we're here!

1261
01:07:57,573 --> 01:08:00,284
Your boyfriend is too competitive.

1262
01:08:00,910 --> 01:08:01,952
All right, guys.

1263
01:08:02,036 --> 01:08:04,455
Let's go through the pitch
one more time. C'mon.

1264
01:08:04,538 --> 01:08:07,625
C, aren't we going home yet?

1265
01:08:08,334 --> 01:08:10,294
I already flipped my underwear.

1266
01:08:10,377 --> 01:08:13,422
And my girlfriend's looking for me.

1267
01:08:13,506 --> 01:08:15,674
And I need to look for a girlfriend.

1268
01:08:16,717 --> 01:08:18,052
What about you?

1269
01:08:18,135 --> 01:08:19,553
Don't you miss your girlfriend?

1270
01:08:40,491 --> 01:08:42,368
So what do you think?

1271
01:08:42,451 --> 01:08:44,078
Um, yes, I agree, sir.

1272
01:08:44,161 --> 01:08:46,831
Actually, it would be best if we--

1273
01:08:46,914 --> 01:08:48,666
We might be up next.

1274
01:08:48,749 --> 01:08:49,667
- Yes.
- Mm-hmm.

1275
01:08:49,750 --> 01:08:51,418
I think we're good to go.

1276
01:08:51,502 --> 01:08:54,463
Remember, confident
but not aggressive, okay?

1277
01:08:54,547 --> 01:08:55,506
Yes.

1278
01:09:27,788 --> 01:09:28,914
You look great.

1279
01:09:34,044 --> 01:09:35,045
You too.

1280
01:09:46,515 --> 01:09:47,933
This won't break us.

1281
01:09:53,898 --> 01:09:55,608
I really meant what I said.

1282
01:09:58,986 --> 01:10:00,863
Then why did you do what you did?

1283
01:10:12,750 --> 01:10:16,921
Guys, shouldn't there be an update
if we got the client or not?

1284
01:10:17,838 --> 01:10:20,090
Followed up, but still no reply.

1285
01:10:20,758 --> 01:10:22,718
Maybe they just can't choose.

1286
01:10:22,801 --> 01:10:24,386
Cheska is really good after all.

1287
01:10:24,470 --> 01:10:25,471
JC…

1288
01:10:26,722 --> 01:10:30,684
Ah, but Cisco is better, of course!

1289
01:10:31,936 --> 01:10:32,978
Dad.

1290
01:10:38,651 --> 01:10:39,985
We'll get this account.

1291
01:10:40,069 --> 01:10:41,237
We better.

1292
01:10:41,320 --> 01:10:45,199
If we want to propel CXC forward,
we need a big client.

1293
01:10:45,282 --> 01:10:48,410
- Maybe we should start--
- Grandpa!

1294
01:10:48,494 --> 01:10:49,536
Dad!

1295
01:10:51,664 --> 01:10:53,582
Guys, my grandfather.

1296
01:10:53,666 --> 01:10:56,043
Our major investor, as you all know.

1297
01:10:56,126 --> 01:10:57,169
And my dad.

1298
01:10:57,962 --> 01:10:59,129
- This is my team, Grandpa.
- Hi, sir!

1299
01:10:59,213 --> 01:11:02,549
- Where's Cheska?
- Sir, Cheska is not part of our team.

1300
01:11:05,094 --> 01:11:07,054
It's an all-boys team.

1301
01:11:07,137 --> 01:11:10,849
I mean, four-and-a-half boys.

1302
01:11:11,684 --> 01:11:13,227
What happened?

1303
01:11:13,310 --> 01:11:14,311
Uh…

1304
01:11:15,312 --> 01:11:17,398
Cheska decided to stay
with the Guinto Group,

1305
01:11:17,481 --> 01:11:18,649
but we will make sure that--

1306
01:11:18,732 --> 01:11:22,861
I agreed to invest in this company
because of Cheska.

1307
01:11:23,696 --> 01:11:25,948
We will manage perfectly without Cheska.

1308
01:11:27,533 --> 01:11:29,702
Your investment will not
go to waste, Grandpa.

1309
01:11:29,785 --> 01:11:31,203
I promise you.

1310
01:11:34,081 --> 01:11:36,834
Bro. Cisco.

1311
01:11:40,129 --> 01:11:41,088
Excuse me.

1312
01:11:41,964 --> 01:11:42,798
What?

1313
01:11:42,881 --> 01:11:45,134
Your son is full of himself.

1314
01:11:45,217 --> 01:11:48,679
He's treading on unfamiliar ground

1315
01:11:48,762 --> 01:11:51,098
and has the stupidity
to surround himself with these idiots.

1316
01:11:53,267 --> 01:11:54,768
We just got our first client.

1317
01:11:56,520 --> 01:11:58,022
I did it without Cheska.

1318
01:11:58,605 --> 01:11:59,940
We beat her.

1319
01:12:00,733 --> 01:12:05,029
You will see that you are
mistaken, Grandpa.

1320
01:12:05,112 --> 01:12:06,572
We'll see.

1321
01:12:07,740 --> 01:12:11,243
Did you hear that?
Sounds like we're getting avocados!

1322
01:12:11,910 --> 01:12:14,621
Congrats to CXC!

1323
01:12:14,705 --> 01:12:18,709
- CXC minus Cheska!
- Minus Cisco too!

1324
01:12:18,792 --> 01:12:20,502
Where is he anyway?

1325
01:12:20,586 --> 01:12:22,087
Did he go with Mookie?

1326
01:12:22,171 --> 01:12:23,005
He was just here!

1327
01:12:23,088 --> 01:12:24,882
Did he join Mookie to pick up Kizzy?

1328
01:12:24,965 --> 01:12:26,300
He's not there.

1329
01:12:26,383 --> 01:12:27,301
Oh, there he is!

1330
01:12:27,384 --> 01:12:29,386
Are you still working?!

1331
01:12:29,470 --> 01:12:32,806
- We should be celebrating already!
- Enough of that!

1332
01:12:33,640 --> 01:12:36,060
Ooh! There's Cheska!

1333
01:12:36,143 --> 01:12:37,353
Look!

1334
01:12:37,436 --> 01:12:40,147
That's cute.

1335
01:12:41,482 --> 01:12:43,776
Aw!

1336
01:12:43,859 --> 01:12:45,110
Bro!

1337
01:12:45,736 --> 01:12:47,279
Congratulations, bro!

1338
01:12:47,363 --> 01:12:48,572
- JC!
- Yes?

1339
01:12:48,655 --> 01:12:50,282
You better stop him!

1340
01:12:50,366 --> 01:12:53,994
They just had a big fight, and now this?

1341
01:12:54,661 --> 01:12:57,247
- They'll both get whiplash!
- Why would I stop him?

1342
01:12:57,331 --> 01:13:00,459
Instead of playing house,
it's better they finally get married!

1343
01:13:00,542 --> 01:13:02,336
That way, they'll be more blessed.

1344
01:13:02,419 --> 01:13:03,754
So I support this!

1345
01:13:03,837 --> 01:13:05,047
But!

1346
01:13:05,964 --> 01:13:08,634
What if Cheska rejects him?

1347
01:13:08,717 --> 01:13:09,760
Um…

1348
01:13:10,594 --> 01:13:12,137
But what if she doesn't?

1349
01:13:12,221 --> 01:13:14,681
That's why he's going to pop her
the question, isn't he?

1350
01:13:15,808 --> 01:13:17,226
You know,

1351
01:13:17,309 --> 01:13:19,228
as a matter of fact,

1352
01:13:19,311 --> 01:13:22,314
they're my inspiration and reason

1353
01:13:22,398 --> 01:13:25,734
as to why my cold heart
has finally melted.

1354
01:13:25,818 --> 01:13:28,570
Looks like I'll be
the next to find love.

1355
01:13:32,866 --> 01:13:35,160
- Are you insane?
- Ouch!

1356
01:13:35,244 --> 01:13:37,621
We have bigger problems right now!

1357
01:13:37,704 --> 01:13:38,914
My goodness!

1358
01:13:40,624 --> 01:13:41,875
You really want to do this now?

1359
01:13:44,837 --> 01:13:46,171
There's no better time than now.

1360
01:13:46,255 --> 01:13:48,006
Double celebration!

1361
01:13:48,090 --> 01:13:49,925
Cheers!

1362
01:13:51,552 --> 01:13:53,470
Well, hurry up!

1363
01:13:53,554 --> 01:13:55,222
- Go to her already!
- That's right.

1364
01:13:55,305 --> 01:13:58,100
- Why are you still here?
- Don't pressure him!

1365
01:13:58,767 --> 01:14:00,144
Scooch over!

1366
01:14:00,227 --> 01:14:03,439
Call her already so she knows!

1367
01:14:03,522 --> 01:14:06,817
Ms. Cheska,
Mr. G is calling you to his office.

1368
01:14:08,360 --> 01:14:09,528
Okay.

1369
01:14:17,578 --> 01:14:18,620
Tuks!

1370
01:14:19,204 --> 01:14:20,998
<i>Tuks, are you done with work?</i>

1371
01:14:21,081 --> 01:14:22,458
Oh yes.

1372
01:14:22,541 --> 01:14:24,084
Mr. G just wants to meet.

1373
01:14:24,168 --> 01:14:25,294
Why?

1374
01:14:25,377 --> 01:14:26,712
Ah…

1375
01:14:26,795 --> 01:14:27,921
To celebrate.

1376
01:14:30,174 --> 01:14:31,884
I'm going to break the news
before Mr. G does.

1377
01:14:33,093 --> 01:14:34,595
CXC won the pitch!

1378
01:14:37,431 --> 01:14:39,099
Congratulations, Tuks!

1379
01:14:41,268 --> 01:14:42,686
I'm sorry.

1380
01:14:42,769 --> 01:14:44,354
You're not mad, are you?

1381
01:14:45,105 --> 01:14:46,148
No.

1382
01:14:46,732 --> 01:14:47,858
You deserve it.

1383
01:14:48,609 --> 01:14:49,776
Thank you.

1384
01:14:51,403 --> 01:14:52,404
So…

1385
01:14:53,363 --> 01:14:55,282
Can I ask you out to dinner tonight?

1386
01:14:56,158 --> 01:14:57,743
So we can celebrate.

1387
01:14:59,244 --> 01:15:01,497
And… talk?

1388
01:15:03,332 --> 01:15:05,167
Yes, Tuks. See you.

1389
01:15:05,250 --> 01:15:06,919
Yes!

1390
01:15:07,002 --> 01:15:09,254
Okay! Marble and Grill tonight?

1391
01:15:09,338 --> 01:15:10,631
I'll see you then.

1392
01:15:10,714 --> 01:15:12,257
<i>Okay, Tuks.</i>

1393
01:15:12,341 --> 01:15:13,634
Okay, perfect.

1394
01:15:14,801 --> 01:15:15,928
I love you, Tukie.

1395
01:15:17,930 --> 01:15:19,181
I love you more.

1396
01:15:22,392 --> 01:15:25,270
<i>I love you more, more, more. Bye-bye!</i>

1397
01:15:31,235 --> 01:15:34,112
My prostate can't handle all this emotion!

1398
01:15:34,196 --> 01:15:35,072
Hey, Cisco!

1399
01:15:35,155 --> 01:15:37,241
From CXC

1400
01:15:37,324 --> 01:15:39,117
to C heart C!

1401
01:15:40,118 --> 01:15:42,621
Cisco, you should shower first!

1402
01:15:42,704 --> 01:15:45,791
Whoo! We can finally celebrate!

1403
01:15:45,874 --> 01:15:47,668
It's them until the end!

1404
01:15:47,751 --> 01:15:49,336
Cheers!

1405
01:15:49,419 --> 01:15:51,338
- Cheers!
- Sorry about them.

1406
01:15:54,091 --> 01:15:55,884
Before you, Cheska,

1407
01:15:56,635 --> 01:15:59,137
I was willing to spend
the rest of my life alone.

1408
01:15:59,221 --> 01:16:01,014
But then you came and I…

1409
01:16:02,307 --> 01:16:03,892
Wine, sir?

1410
01:16:04,518 --> 01:16:05,727
Sorry, hold on.

1411
01:16:08,230 --> 01:16:11,400
You'd think this was a pitch.
Cisco, just relax!

1412
01:16:12,651 --> 01:16:15,362
You're right. Sorry.

1413
01:16:25,539 --> 01:16:26,415
Mookie!

1414
01:16:26,498 --> 01:16:30,252
<i>Hello, Cisco.</i>
<i>Have you checked your email?</i>

1415
01:16:30,335 --> 01:16:32,087
Huh? What email?

1416
01:16:32,170 --> 01:16:34,047
<i>The one from…</i>

1417
01:16:34,131 --> 01:16:35,882
They just sent it now?

1418
01:16:37,092 --> 01:16:38,343
All right, I'll check it now.

1419
01:16:51,315 --> 01:16:52,482
Hi, Tuks!

1420
01:16:53,859 --> 01:16:56,153
Tukie, my head hurts again--

1421
01:16:56,236 --> 01:16:57,237
You knew about this?

1422
01:16:58,864 --> 01:17:00,073
About what?

1423
01:17:02,075 --> 01:17:04,661
"Different direction
with a different agency

1424
01:17:04,745 --> 01:17:06,455
to fit our brand best."

1425
01:17:08,915 --> 01:17:10,917
You're the different agency?

1426
01:17:16,757 --> 01:17:17,758
Fuck.

1427
01:17:20,302 --> 01:17:21,678
Cisco, can we talk at home--

1428
01:17:21,762 --> 01:17:22,638
Plot twist!

1429
01:17:24,056 --> 01:17:25,140
Seems rigged, huh?

1430
01:17:27,017 --> 01:17:27,893
Bill, please.

1431
01:17:27,976 --> 01:17:29,728
I can pay.

1432
01:17:32,064 --> 01:17:33,273
So what happened?

1433
01:17:34,816 --> 01:17:36,610
The client was mine, but now they're not.

1434
01:17:36,693 --> 01:17:37,819
What did you guys do?

1435
01:17:41,990 --> 01:17:44,576
What did you do that
changed the client's mind?

1436
01:17:45,202 --> 01:17:47,996
Was it Shane's doing? Or Mr. G's?

1437
01:17:48,080 --> 01:17:49,748
Cheska!

1438
01:17:51,541 --> 01:17:52,751
Did you enjoy it?

1439
01:17:52,834 --> 01:17:54,419
You're happy you beat me, aren't you?

1440
01:17:54,503 --> 01:17:56,254
It's Shane, isn't it?

1441
01:17:56,338 --> 01:17:58,882
That asshole has been setting me up
for failure since day one!

1442
01:17:58,965 --> 01:17:59,966
That's not true.

1443
01:18:00,967 --> 01:18:02,594
So now you're siding with them?

1444
01:18:02,678 --> 01:18:04,846
Cheska, they forced me out of G Spot!

1445
01:18:05,472 --> 01:18:07,265
Was that not enough for them?

1446
01:18:07,349 --> 01:18:10,310
They're kicking me while I'm down,
and you're just letting them.

1447
01:18:10,394 --> 01:18:12,396
Talk to me!

1448
01:18:12,938 --> 01:18:15,941
I've already been screwed over,
and now you're making me look stupid?

1449
01:18:16,608 --> 01:18:18,318
Don't you feel bad?
Aren't you guilty?

1450
01:18:18,402 --> 01:18:19,653
What do you want from me?

1451
01:18:19,736 --> 01:18:21,863
- The truth!
- You can't handle it.

1452
01:18:23,115 --> 01:18:24,366
What do you mean?

1453
01:18:24,449 --> 01:18:25,951
Why can't I handle the truth?

1454
01:18:26,034 --> 01:18:28,495
Cheska! You think
I can't handle the truth?

1455
01:18:28,578 --> 01:18:30,997
- You guys stole the client from me!
- We didn't steal anything!

1456
01:18:31,081 --> 01:18:34,209
- You took that account from me!
- I gave it up for you!

1457
01:18:36,211 --> 01:18:39,214
They chose me, not you!

1458
01:18:39,297 --> 01:18:40,132
Liar!

1459
01:18:40,215 --> 01:18:41,925
It's the truth, Cisco!

1460
01:18:42,718 --> 01:18:45,095
I won that account!

1461
01:18:45,178 --> 01:18:47,973
But I made up
this bullshit excuse to the client

1462
01:18:48,056 --> 01:18:49,808
so it would go to you instead.

1463
01:18:51,893 --> 01:18:55,897
I practically sabotaged my career

1464
01:18:56,940 --> 01:18:58,650
just so you would win.

1465
01:19:00,360 --> 01:19:01,528
I don't believe you.

1466
01:19:02,696 --> 01:19:04,156
I don't believe you!

1467
01:19:06,908 --> 01:19:08,076
Wow.

1468
01:19:08,910 --> 01:19:11,288
I'm not sure which is more insulting.

1469
01:19:15,208 --> 01:19:18,086
That you think that I cheated,

1470
01:19:18,170 --> 01:19:20,714
or that you'd rather
believe that I cheated

1471
01:19:20,797 --> 01:19:23,967
than accept that I won that account
because I am just as good as you!

1472
01:19:24,050 --> 01:19:26,344
Or maybe even better!

1473
01:19:34,186 --> 01:19:37,522
Are you always going to be like this
whenever I beat you?

1474
01:19:39,107 --> 01:19:41,234
If I'm the one winning,

1475
01:19:41,318 --> 01:19:43,570
can you be happy for me?

1476
01:19:45,113 --> 01:19:47,073
If I outgrow you,

1477
01:19:47,157 --> 01:19:48,700
can you accept that?

1478
01:19:52,120 --> 01:19:54,372
When I do better than you or outdo you…

1479
01:19:56,583 --> 01:19:58,210
can you still love me?

1480
01:19:59,419 --> 01:20:01,630
You want to be the only winner.

1481
01:20:03,048 --> 01:20:04,591
You want to be the only one at the top.

1482
01:20:06,051 --> 01:20:07,135
But how about me?

1483
01:20:11,264 --> 01:20:13,099
You just want me to clap for you.

1484
01:20:16,228 --> 01:20:19,064
Is this the only version of us
that works for you?

1485
01:20:21,399 --> 01:20:26,404
All my love, all my sacrifices,

1486
01:20:27,697 --> 01:20:28,990
all that?

1487
01:20:31,701 --> 01:20:32,702
For this?

1488
01:20:36,873 --> 01:20:37,874
For you?

1489
01:20:43,463 --> 01:20:44,923
Now I'm wondering…

1490
01:20:49,261 --> 01:20:51,096
do you even deserve my love?

1491
01:20:57,060 --> 01:20:58,478
Do you even love me?

1492
01:21:37,851 --> 01:21:39,060
Cisco…

1493
01:22:12,135 --> 01:22:13,136
Cheska!

1494
01:23:02,686 --> 01:23:05,689
Cisco, Mela is really
against the DBS treatment.

1495
01:23:05,772 --> 01:23:07,148
- We don't--
- Give me that.

1496
01:23:07,232 --> 01:23:08,149
Cisco.

1497
01:23:09,234 --> 01:23:11,778
Our daughter has been in a coma
for two years now.

1498
01:23:12,988 --> 01:23:18,118
We're thankful for all your financial help
and the sacrifices you've made

1499
01:23:18,201 --> 01:23:20,704
ever since Cheska had the aneurysm.

1500
01:23:20,787 --> 01:23:24,582
We know you mean well

1501
01:23:24,666 --> 01:23:27,544
and only want the best for Cheska.

1502
01:23:27,627 --> 01:23:33,258
But that experimental DBS treatment
that you keep bringing up…

1503
01:23:34,009 --> 01:23:37,804
They're just going
to open her head up again!

1504
01:23:38,972 --> 01:23:41,433
She almost died last time!

1505
01:23:42,142 --> 01:23:45,520
What if she doesn't make it this time?

1506
01:23:45,603 --> 01:23:47,480
I won't risk my daughter's life!

1507
01:23:47,564 --> 01:23:51,484
So whatever it is
you're thinking of trying, stop!

1508
01:23:51,568 --> 01:23:53,611
But please--

1509
01:25:10,146 --> 01:25:12,273
Is this about the DBS?

1510
01:25:15,902 --> 01:25:19,614
Cheska's parents told me that
they've finally made a decision.

1511
01:25:19,697 --> 01:25:21,616
Why are you still forcing it?

1512
01:25:22,325 --> 01:25:24,494
I don't want to regret anything.

1513
01:25:26,037 --> 01:25:27,789
Mr. G, you know us.

1514
01:25:29,749 --> 01:25:31,459
You know how much I loved her.

1515
01:25:32,293 --> 01:25:33,419
Yes.

1516
01:25:35,338 --> 01:25:37,882
And I saw how much she loved you too.

1517
01:25:40,093 --> 01:25:42,053
More than you probably ever know.

1518
01:25:48,226 --> 01:25:50,770
I will tell you some things
that will hurt.

1519
01:25:54,357 --> 01:25:56,025
But you need to hear them.

1520
01:25:58,278 --> 01:26:00,029
<i> You almost declined your promotion</i>

1521
01:26:00,113 --> 01:26:02,740
because you were too afraid
to hurt his feelings.

1522
01:26:03,533 --> 01:26:07,620
And now you let go of this big
of an account and opportunity?

1523
01:26:08,872 --> 01:26:10,915
May I remind you, Cheska,

1524
01:26:11,708 --> 01:26:14,169
this is for the company.

1525
01:26:14,252 --> 01:26:16,546
Not just for you
and definitely not for Cisco.

1526
01:26:16,629 --> 01:26:19,132
Mr. G, I'm just worried
I won't handle the load--

1527
01:26:21,509 --> 01:26:22,719
I know you.

1528
01:26:24,596 --> 01:26:25,972
If you really wanted it,

1529
01:26:26,639 --> 01:26:28,099
nothing would stop you.

1530
01:26:44,365 --> 01:26:48,328
I know what it's like
to dim your own light

1531
01:26:49,162 --> 01:26:50,747
to let your partner shine.

1532
01:26:51,915 --> 01:26:53,958
To make yourself smaller.

1533
01:26:55,877 --> 01:26:58,963
So that you could make
the person that you love

1534
01:26:59,964 --> 01:27:02,717
feel like… he's enough.

1535
01:27:04,219 --> 01:27:06,554
To completely lose yourself

1536
01:27:07,513 --> 01:27:09,641
just to continue loving him.

1537
01:27:13,645 --> 01:27:17,106
Cheska, I know
how difficult this is for you,

1538
01:27:18,524 --> 01:27:21,819
but the company also needs this account.

1539
01:27:22,570 --> 01:27:23,863
We deserve this win.

1540
01:27:23,947 --> 01:27:25,490
You deserve this win.

1541
01:27:27,784 --> 01:27:29,369
You worked so hard for this.

1542
01:27:30,995 --> 01:27:34,207
And so did the rest of your team.

1543
01:27:40,546 --> 01:27:43,758
And I will get this account back,

1544
01:27:43,841 --> 01:27:46,135
whether you approve of it or not.

1545
01:27:47,387 --> 01:27:48,638
Mr. G.

1546
01:27:50,515 --> 01:27:54,018
Is it okay if we outsource
one execution to their team?

1547
01:27:56,354 --> 01:27:58,147
Let Cisco be the director.

1548
01:27:58,982 --> 01:28:00,066
He's still the best.

1549
01:28:01,109 --> 01:28:02,986
Unbelievable.

1550
01:28:06,990 --> 01:28:08,700
Okay, fine.

1551
01:28:12,078 --> 01:28:13,663
Thank you, Mr. G.

1552
01:28:15,873 --> 01:28:17,333
I'm sorry.

1553
01:28:23,965 --> 01:28:25,466
She was selfless.

1554
01:28:27,135 --> 01:28:28,386
But I guess

1555
01:28:30,221 --> 01:28:32,348
she never got to tell you that.

1556
01:28:32,432 --> 01:28:34,100
Even that final win?

1557
01:28:36,102 --> 01:28:39,814
Something that she can claim
solely as her own?

1558
01:28:41,357 --> 01:28:43,818
She was willing to share that with you.

1559
01:28:43,901 --> 01:28:45,653
That's how much she loved you.

1560
01:28:47,530 --> 01:28:49,282
I don't deserve her.

1561
01:28:52,368 --> 01:28:55,163
I know you love her too.
I never doubted that.

1562
01:28:57,332 --> 01:28:59,125
But this thing that you're doing,

1563
01:29:01,461 --> 01:29:04,172
forcing Cheska to wake up?

1564
01:29:06,132 --> 01:29:07,383
Ask yourself.

1565
01:29:08,801 --> 01:29:10,595
Who are you really doing it for?

1566
01:29:12,347 --> 01:29:15,933
If Cheska lives, then she lives.

1567
01:29:17,268 --> 01:29:18,519
And if she does,

1568
01:29:20,688 --> 01:29:25,026
is this the version of Cisco
that you want her to wake up to?

1569
01:29:28,821 --> 01:29:32,200
If you really want to apologize to her,

1570
01:29:33,159 --> 01:29:36,704
then be the man that she loved

1571
01:29:36,788 --> 01:29:39,707
and she believed that you could be.

1572
01:30:08,194 --> 01:30:09,362
I was worried.

1573
01:30:29,132 --> 01:30:30,299
Hi, Tuks.

1574
01:30:33,594 --> 01:30:35,263
It's me again.

1575
01:30:38,891 --> 01:30:43,396
Not to pressure you to come back already,

1576
01:30:43,479 --> 01:30:48,442
but… to promise that
I will be a better man.

1577
01:30:51,028 --> 01:30:53,531
A man truly worthy of your love.

1578
01:31:01,581 --> 01:31:02,999
I'm sorry, Tuks.

1579
01:31:05,626 --> 01:31:07,461
I hope you can forgive me.

1580
01:31:11,090 --> 01:31:12,675
I'm sorry for…

1581
01:31:16,053 --> 01:31:20,641
Not just what I said and what I did
the last time we were together.

1582
01:31:25,688 --> 01:31:30,193
I'm sorry for all the times that
I didn't treat you right.

1583
01:31:35,239 --> 01:31:37,617
For all the times that I hurt you.

1584
01:31:42,455 --> 01:31:46,167
For the times that I was… selfish.

1585
01:31:48,836 --> 01:31:52,256
You had to make yourself smaller

1586
01:31:52,340 --> 01:31:56,844
just so I could feel loved by you.

1587
01:32:04,310 --> 01:32:07,104
I'm sorry I didn't see that before, Tuks.

1588
01:32:12,235 --> 01:32:14,862
I'm sorry I forgot that you loved me.

1589
01:32:21,577 --> 01:32:24,205
I'm sorry I forgot that I loved you.

1590
01:32:28,417 --> 01:32:30,628
I will keep on waiting for you.

1591
01:32:33,714 --> 01:32:34,924
I love you.

1592
01:32:39,845 --> 01:32:41,264
I love you more.

1593
01:32:45,935 --> 01:32:47,353
I love you more.

